C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T11:25:31-08:00","id":1355031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1355010#post1355010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every Tremere yearns to kill his sire, sire's sire, and sire's sire to rebuild the Clan from the ashes.<br /> <br /> It's the Sith way.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reading would make House Carna something like the Nigthsisters, which is an interesting read and still works. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=scE9WhN9TjY\" data-code=\"scE9WhN9TjY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/scE9WhN9TjY/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T14:52:30-08:00","id":1355060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilbyTheFat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1355007#post1355007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say so. The members of Houses Tremere, Carna &amp; Goratrix are all loyal to the vision of how <i>they</i> want the Clan to be, but the Ipsissimus Tremere just wanna do their own thing and don't strike me as the type to give a shit about the Clan as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Let me break it down for you<br /> <br /> &quot;House Tremere&quot;, obviously loyal to house Tremere what with all the selective recruitment and the pyramid's social reinforcement and the bonds... <br /> <br /> Goratrix: Destroyed. The ones who survived are of course, loyal to the clan, though some of them may not know it yet...<br /> <br /> Hactivists: You mean to learn Thaumaturgy over the net you need to give blood to a computer and voluntarily submit to an unknown Dominate?<br /> <br /> &quot;Ipsissimus&quot; A rebranding so that Tremere could operate freely in Anarch territories; Quashing rival bloodmages and all that. <br /> <br /> Carna: A trap to weed out the mistakes (If you wanna actually pretend this house could ever happen within the context of the Tremere) <br /> <br /> Telyav: <br /> *Smug Tremere contempt *<br /> &quot;Presence, Pagan magic, a fear of religious symbols? This is either a bloodline of Baali or Ventrue or some Caitiff had delusions of Grandeur&quot;. <br /> <br /> Conclusion: The pyramid is absolute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T15:11:24-08:00","id":1355064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1355060#post1355060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;House Tremere&quot;, obviously loyal to house Tremere what with all the selective recruitment and the pyramid's social reinforcement and the bonds...<br /> <br /> Goratrix: Destroyed. The ones who survived are of course, loyal to the clan, though some of them may not know it yet...<br /> <br /> Hactivists: You mean to learn Thaumaturgy over the net you need to give blood to a computer and voluntarily submit to an unknown Dominate?<br /> <br /> &quot;Ipsissimus&quot; A rebranding so that Tremere could operate freely in Anarch territories; Quashing rival bloodmages and all that.<br /> <br /> Carna: A trap to weed out the mistakes (If you wanna actually pretend this house could ever happen within the context of the Tremere)<br /> <br /> Telyav:<br /> *Smug Tremere contempt *<br /> &quot;Presence, Pagan magic, a fear of religious symbols? This is either a bloodline of Baali or Ventrue or some Caitiff had delusions of Grandeur&quot;.<br /> <br /> Conclusion: The pyramid is absolute.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Pyramid was kept together via a Blood Bond to the Council of Seven that constantly played its members against one another and instilled an everlasting hatred for other members while a toadying sycopancy to the Seven.<br /> <br /> Then the Seven died.<br /> <br /> Now the Tremere can't blood bond anyone.<br /> <br /> My headcanon is it's like a set of dominoes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T15:56:10-08:00","id":1355075,"title":"","content":"You don't need magic powers to make an effective pyramid scheme, and a clan has always been like a union. The sociology/psychology behind it all would suggest that you could video yourself Diablerizing Tremere and the Co7 in front of a live audience and you'd still not shake the pyramid; it has a strong foundation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T16:09:59-08:00","id":1355079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1355075#post1355075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need magic powers to make an effective pyramid scheme, and a clan has always been like a union. The sociology/psychology behind it all would suggest that you could video yourself Diablerizing Tremere and the Co7 in front of a live audience and you'd still not shake the pyramid; it has a strong foundation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's the thing about V:TM, everyone's table is different.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T18:12:07-08:00","id":1355306,"title":"","content":"* As mentioned elsewhere, Marcus Vitel manipulated Theo Bell into killing Hardestadt, and conspired with other Ventrue in the event which is how it happened and how Bell was able to escape.<br /> <br /> * Fort Worth has one prince, Dallas has a different one.<br /> <br /> * Vancouver is still independent - the Camarilla calls it Anarch, but this is not really true.<br /> <br /> And here is a dark one...<br /> <br /> * None of the Nazi high command were ever made into vampires, and only a couple of the Nazi's made into Nazi's have survived into modern times. The supposed appearance of &quot;famous&quot; Nazi's as vampires is the result of a Tzimisce with Dementation (or a Malkavian with Vicissitude) who has been taking Nazi sympathizers and wanna-bes and literally turning them into Nazis, inside and out. This is how something like a half-dozen Goebbelshave appeared across the last 70 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T18:19:01-08:00","id":1355307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1355306#post1355306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* None of the Nazi high command were ever made into vampires, and only a couple of the Nazi's made into Nazi's have survived into modern times. The supposed appearance of &quot;famous&quot; Nazi's as vampires is the result of a Tzimisce with Dementation (or a Malkavian with Vicissitude) who has been taking Nazi sympathizers and wanna-bes and literally turning them into Nazis, inside and out. This is how something like a half-dozen Goebbelshave appeared across the last 70 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually did that in my games with Berlin by Night. There was ONE vampire involved with the Nazis in the 10th generation Brujah Dieter who was a huge Hitler fanboy and served as his bodyguard for much of the war, sadly thwarting many supernatural attempts on Hitler.<br /> <br /> Even the Sabbat find him a joke for his loyalty to a failed Kine ideology.<br /> <br /> His 4th Reich is composed of wannabes and losers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-16-2019, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T22:52:14-08:00","id":1355341,"title":"","content":"You should start this thread on the White Wolf Reddit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T11:11:58-08:00","id":1355443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1352280#post1352280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sabbat</b><br /> <br /> + The Sabbat lost a lot of their strategic reserve in the Gehenna Crusade and most die-hard fanatics as well as followers. They also have suffered major losses in South America to the Drowned, Mexico City, Montreal, and so on due to the Second Inquisition. Many defected to the Anarchs, though. They're not dead as a sect, just dramatically weakened. Having gone from the Soviet Union to the Camarilla to their North Korea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we talking in terms of cannon fodder, or someone with training and experience (inasmuch as the Sabbat cultivates that). I could see the latter, not necessarily the former. And even in the caes of the latter I expect the weakness would only be temporary until they started a crash program to bolster their ranks (those that survive as cannon fodder probably climb up the ladder pretty quick given rapid promotion and the kind of culture the Sabbat thrived on.) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Beckoning</b><br /> <br /> + The Beckoning tends to only affect Elders who are over 1000 years old and/or 6th generation or below. Even then, it's about 1 out of 3 who are affected so far.<br /> <br /> + The Beckoning summons vampires to the deserts of Saudi Arabia where satellite footage is corrupted and very few people return.<br /> <br /> + Those Elders who do resist it suffer the Withering and start to lose much of their greater powers.<br /> <br /> + The Beckoning is due to the 1000 year Gehenna Cycle. The Antediluvians are summoning their eldest and strongest childer to either feed themselves or grow stronger. </div> </div> </div>Maybe rather than all at once (as per the original 'Gehenna' book) God's curse/retribution stretched over a much longer period (Because said deity was always presented as kinda an asshole, and collateral damage as 'punishment' for sinful ways might fit that MO) and it happens in stages (withering first, then beckoning) which build off each other in different ways. The Antes triggering the beckoning is perhaps an attempt to break free or fight back against the curse (and God.) Is Caine leading it? Does he oppose it? Does he care or is he even around? Who knows. Or maybe its Lilith manipulating things behind the scenes (I'm borrowing from Gehenna with this one, but.. why not?) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> + The Antediluvians are feeding on the Sabbat but allowing some of them to feed on their &quot;favored&quot; childer that makes them 5th to 6th generation and able to stay awake. Like Mithras being eaten by Monty Coven, his higher generation helps him stay awake and adapt to the modern era. </div> </div> </div>Or the Sabbat is under a different faction of Antediluvians trying to oppose the ones you describe above. <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1352287#post1352287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are other ancient terrors, besides the Antedeluvian Blood Gods, manipulating vampire politics and the jyhad. For the night is dark, and full of terrors... well beyond vampires.<br /> ...<br /> Eastern vampires, and vampire like creatures across the Pacific and into the Americas, are not related to Caine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a return to the pre-KOTE approach where (like KotEK) they're a variation of Cainites (or something akin to the 'Alphas' of Supernatural.) No reason it couldn't work - maybe they resulted from a different progenitor who was cursed differently and evolved themselves in a different way (differences in belief, etc.) The Kuei-Jin stuff may just be their way of trying to treat themselvs as different/better than Cainites, despite actually having similar origins. Hell you could even still do some of the similar things (Salubri have that power to feed on blood/breath from other beings, and life/energy stealing isn't unique to the K-J.) And maybe the other originators of a line got tired of Caine's shit and decided to do something about it. <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1352342#post1352342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Relatedly, in my headcanon, more than thirteen 3rd generation vampires survived the flood. Some never Embraced, some only Embraced a very small number of kindred, some died post-Flood, and some went into torpor because of the flood and never made it out. The big thirteen are just the prolific ones. My players are aware there's possibly more hidden uber-monsters out there, but thus far have only found hints, rumors, speculation and oddities that both back up and contradict it all. I have no plans to really use these &quot;missing Antediluvians&quot;, but I like having them exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this was a thing in Gehenna too. Not all of them necessarily are monsters though. Some could be resisting the monsters (for good or for personal reasons) whereas others may simply be pursuing their own inscrutable goals to survive or 'ascend/evolve' (see the Shaper from Gehenna.) <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1352465#post1352465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">+ The Second Inquisition is composed of an alliance of the Knights Templar, Judges, Inquisition, various Muslim groups, CDC scientists, SAD, an NSA subgroup, and several CIA black ops groups. It has also recruited the surviving Hunters and a bunch of Technocracy acolytes who form various conspiracies they didn't know answered back to supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given this takes place in 2018 I tend to think that the original Imbued would either organize into more distinct factions (think of what happens in Hunter: the Vigil) or would get put under the second inquisition or Project Twilight (if not both) which was something touched on in HtR: First Contact. Given something like two decades for the Imbued Hunters to 'evolve' from 'normal people' into hardened fighters, and given their Dark Age ties to the inquisition (and numina/True Faith) I think you could see them becoming foot soldiers in the Second Inquisition even if they didn't come directly under the command of the Society. Heck, perhaps you have your own factions (varying degrees of secularism and religious) that make up such people. Imbued would be something like the 'elite' but I think there would be room for lots of lesser kinds (Hedge magicians, true faith, psychics, and other kinds of numina like from Hunters Hunted and such) since its all 'human power' The Imbued are sort of just 'hyper numina' of their own methinks. <br /> <br /> I could see Technocratic factions backing the second inquisition as part of their own efforts through various channels, but I don't think they'd want to tip their own hand lest they becomes targets (And they probably have other priorities as well.) Providing better gear, intel, funding, perhaps guiding their use of numina and helping to track down/train imbued for example. Some of it may even be influence of other vampirs to use as tools against adversaries (including other Antediluvians) which furthers the idea that there is a sort of 'internal power struggle' between different factions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> + There's about 5000 to 7000 or so members total and its threat is somewhat exaggerated. It seems omnipresent due to the below and their access to mundane resources combined with Kindred paranoia.<br /> <br /> + Whenever the Second Inquisition was sending hordes of well-armed soldiers with no regards to casualties into vampire lairs or engaged in shoot-outs in the street, that's actually the Technocracy because they don't have accountability, limits on their funding, or a problem just cloning some new Men in Black or HIT marks. </div> </div> </div>I could actually see these two as related. Another reason the Technocracy might back the 2I is because its 'cover' for their own actions and stuff they could help build on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> + The &quot;Hellsing&quot; Group of the Union is a relatively small group of fanatics in the Union who went that way due to Ravnos. They don't control the Second Inquisition but are patronizing it like Marcus Vitel and taking advantage of it.<br /> <br /> It's mostly a combination of the former Invictus group and John Courage's friends having found a new windmill to tilt. </div> </div> </div>Sounds a bit like the British Men of Letters from Supernatural as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1352681#post1352681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nephilim were the Damphyr children of Zillah and a Fallen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Dunno if I'd try to pin nephilim entirely on vampires. Maybe one TYPE of nephilim came from Vampires, like others could come from werewolves, or fae, or so on. It would also have to be human and vampire to technically be a 'dhampir', so unless it was a human thrall or an embodied fallen it would be getting away from teh strict definition. I'm also not sure I'd tie it to Zillah since by oWoD how you get a 'dhampir' is technically someone who is at least thin blood. I don't think it would HAVE to be 15th-16th generation per se - they just happen to be the most ready source of thin bloods. But an older generation who was thin blooded could probably produce them. Hell Giovanni chronicle had a 6th generation who had a flaw in his vampire curse where he still aged (would die at age 1000) so that would suggest you could have Thin Bloods at least up to the elder stage (possibly 5th if we go by game mechanics I suppose.) <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1352474#post1352474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all of the Second Inquisition's rampaging, there are still whole colonies of Gargoyles out there. This is because Gargoyles are cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if it can be leveraged for crossover purposes as Grumpy notes, even better. There's considerabel crossover potential with the concept as well (Changeling, Mage, etc.) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Half the Antedeluvians have, at one time or another over the ages, decided that the best way to survive the Jyhad is to develop their signature disciplines to the point where they can become something other than a vampire. It remains to be seen whether any of them have transcended their respective curses well enough to have avoided the Gehenna War. </div> </div> </div>Again sounds alot like one of the Gehenna plotlines (again the Shaper comes to mind) so this strikes me as completely plausible. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1352658#post1352658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My headcanon is that Augustus Giovanni has been sealed in a coffin belonging to one of the Apostles and is now buried under the Vatican. Presumably to Indiana Jones music.<br /> <br /> Now is that a GOOD thing or a BAD thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>If he's (metaphorically) shitting himself in terror and going insane? Its good. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1353687#post1353687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[+ Most vampires gradually start to become pansexual due to the fact Feeding and Sex are intrinsically linked in their minds. Some vampires remain either strongly heterosexual or homosexual but this is due to personal identity that most discard with time. Asexual vampires feel the Hunger as something as a wholly alien desire.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has the feel of an Anne Rice tie in. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> + All vampires are physically capable of sex with the Blush of Life and enjoy it if they're so inclined to do so in life. However, the experience of sex pales to the feeding and most find sex without feeding unsatisfying.<br /> <br /> + Vampires are capable of ghouling through their use of fluids during sex. This is one of the few &quot;covert&quot; means of ghouling or blood bonding someone. </div> </div> </div>Ghouling via sex is an intresting idea. Wonder why they never thought of it before, given it would fit in perfectly with the concept. Incidentally how would the Revenant and Dhampir concepts fit in with this?<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1354851#post1354851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* The Wan Kuei are pretty much their own collection of Kindred clans with a lot of them trained in Spirit Thaumaturgy or Disciplines that allow them to manipulate spirit.<br /> <br /> * The Nagaraja are a major Clan there rather than a Bloodline and have no connection to the Euthantos. That's just a rumor they spread while manipulating the Black Hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>These two seem like they would naturally correlate. Especially since getting sustenance from flesh was also part of KoTE. Also dovetails with Grumpy's idea in the same vein. <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1354890#post1354890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there are any gargoyles left at Ceoris. I think all they gargoyles are hanging out at a castle put on top of a skyscraper in Manhattan by a scheming billionaire. But having gargoyles sleep under the water has possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>You beat me to this reference, alas. But I still like the crossover potential. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1354946#post1354946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* The Succubus Club is full of Hollow Ones. Helena has no idea she's actually in danger there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they're all mages, or because they might fetishize Gothic Horror? <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1355010#post1355010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every Tremere yearns to kill his sire, sire's sire, and sire's sire to rebuild the Clan from the ashes.<br /> <br /> It's the Sith way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could also see one side trying to weaponize hedge magic and awakened mages - they reverse-reverse engineer thautmaturgy to get something like their original archaic sorcery and create a ritual to locate awakaned Orphans, and then train them as weapons against the other mages. It would be like the archaic sorcerers the True Black Hand had. This also strikes me as a great time for the Order of Hermes to engage in a Shadow Massassa War. Have the Order playing all sides against each other to further their destruction once they discover one of the Tremere factions has been poaching orphans (the Order might also try to 'recover' such beings or recruit them - either faking their deaths or using them as double agents.) <br /> <br /> Perhaps you even have some Tremere who are tired of being vampires and are bargaining hoping the Order can reverse the process (whether they can or not is up for debate.) <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1355306#post1355306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* None of the Nazi high command were ever made into vampires, and only a couple of the Nazi's made into Nazi's have survived into modern times. The supposed appearance of &quot;famous&quot; Nazi's as vampires is the result of a Tzimisce with Dementation (or a Malkavian with Vicissitude) who has been taking Nazi sympathizers and wanna-bes and literally turning them into Nazis, inside and out. This is how something like a half-dozen Goebbelshave appeared across the last 70 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they invade London at any point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T13:58:30-08:00","id":1355485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1355443#post1355443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they invade London at any point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T14:17:37-08:00","id":1355492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1355443#post1355443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we talking in terms of cannon fodder, or someone with training and experience (inasmuch as the Sabbat cultivates that). I could see the latter, not necessarily the former. And even in the caes of the latter I expect the weakness would only be temporary until they started a crash program to bolster their ranks (those that survive as cannon fodder probably climb up the ladder pretty quick given rapid promotion and the kind of culture the Sabbat thrived on.)</div> </div> </div> </div>In my headcanon, the Sabbat remaining aren't necessarily planning any Crusades but consolidating what they have left. Under assault from the Second Inquisition, Drowned, Lasombra Civil War, and their own deranged Gehenna Crusaders possessed by millennia old vampires, they've been avoiding quantity over quality. The survivors are thinking it might be better to try to stick to well-trained soldiers ala the Black Hand versus packs of feral animals. Right now, shovelheads barely kept in line by the Vinculum are a liability rather than a strength. They've even been, ugh, observing the Masquerade more thoroughly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe rather than all at once (as per the original 'Gehenna' book) God's curse/retribution stretched over a much longer period (Because said deity was always presented as kinda an asshole, and collateral damage as 'punishment' for sinful ways might fit that MO) and it happens in stages (withering first, then beckoning) which build off each other in different ways. The Antes triggering the beckoning is perhaps an attempt to break free or fight back against the curse (and God.) Is Caine leading it? Does he oppose it? Does he care or is he even around? Who knows. Or maybe its Lilith manipulating things behind the scenes (I'm borrowing from Gehenna with this one, but.. why not?) </div> </div> </div>In last night's game, I had Mithras state he has survived multiple Gehennas and that the trigger for it was the Thin Bloods showing the Curse of Caine has thinned past the 13th generation it was to be passed down upon. Eventually, they would eat their way up the food chain or be rewarded by the Antediluvians or destroyed. The Antediluvians summon their food to them, they feed and they spare some while destroying others. Unlike what many vampires feared, its the youngest of their kind who have the least to fear. If they survive until the next cycle, maybe they'll be worth eating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or the Sabbat is under a different faction of Antediluvians trying to oppose the ones you describe above. </div> </div> </div>One reason I had the Ministry falling apart was the Setites got Beckoned too and the fact that they ended up dying or getting eaten too caused many to wonder if Set was anything different than the others. Hesha lost his faith because he found the Enoch sarcaphogus in BJD and it pretty much told him that the FoS' version of thing was wrong.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sounds like a return to the pre-KOTE approach where (like KotEK) they're a variation of Cainites (or something akin to the 'Alphas' of Supernatural.) No reason it couldn't work - maybe they resulted from a different progenitor who was cursed differently and evolved themselves in a different way (differences in belief, etc.) The Kuei-Jin stuff may just be their way of trying to treat themselvs as different/better than Cainites, despite actually having similar origins. Hell you could even still do some of the similar things (Salubri have that power to feed on blood/breath from other beings, and life/energy stealing isn't unique to the K-J.) And maybe the other originators of a line got tired of Caine's shit and decided to do something about it. </div> </div> </div>A very good idea and interpretation of what I was going for.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given this takes place in 2018 I tend to think that the original Imbued would either organize into more distinct factions (think of what happens in Hunter: the Vigil) or would get put under the second inquisition or Project Twilight (if not both) which was something touched on in HtR: First Contact. Given something like two decades for the Imbued Hunters to 'evolve' from 'normal people' into hardened fighters, and given their Dark Age ties to the inquisition (and numina/True Faith) I think you could see them becoming foot soldiers in the Second Inquisition even if they didn't come directly under the command of the Society. Heck, perhaps you have your own factions (varying degrees of secularism and religious) that make up such people. Imbued would be something like the 'elite' but I think there would be room for lots of lesser kinds (Hedge magicians, true faith, psychics, and other kinds of numina like from Hunters Hunted and such) since its all 'human power' The Imbued are sort of just 'hyper numina' of their own methinks. </div> </div> </div>One way to handle it is that a few thousand Imbued were created under the Red Star, slaughtered a bunch of monsters (mostly Wraiths and Risen) but no one really was Imbued afterward to replace them. Thus, they've been steadily lowering in number ever since. It makes them wonder if they were meant solely as a response to, say, the Demon: The Fallen situation and whoever made them never meant for them to be a faction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I could actually see these two as related. Another reason the Technocracy might back the 2I is because its 'cover' for their own actions and stuff they could help build on. </div> </div> </div>Even with their tenuous truce with the Traditions, the Technocracy has Threat Null, the Nephandi, the Marauders, and who knows what else so I think they can throw stuff at the vampire &quot;threat&quot; (especially after Ravnos showed them vampires can be bigger issues than a few dead extra homeless people in every city (as their Comptrollers previously dismissed the undead). You could also have them subtly convincing the various agencies to keep blankbodies under wraps.<br /> <br /> <b>NWO Secretary: </b><i>*Mind 3*</i>I think it's a bad idea to reveal the supernatural to the public. It could cause a panic. Here's your coffee.<br /> <br /> <b>Second Inquisition Boss:</b> I think it's a bad idea to reveal the supernatural to the public. It could cause a panic. Thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If he's (metaphorically) shitting himself in terror and going insane? Its good. </div> </div> </div>The only Antediluvian to be utterly helpless as there are no ghosts, no minds to dominate, or strength to break the confines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ghouling via sex is an intresting idea. Wonder why they never thought of it before, given it would fit in perfectly with the concept. Incidentally how would the Revenant and Dhampir concepts fit in with this? </div> </div> </div>I have it in my rules that vampires can have sex but they can only sire children the old fashioned way with rituals. That's a key component to making Revenants.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because they're all mages, or because they might fetishize Gothic Horror? </div> </div> </div>\u200bI always treated Hollow Ones as more serious than most other M:TA fans. Yes, 90% of them are Goths but that's because they're Orphans of the modern era living in the World of Darkness. They're DIY mages and that lends itself to being dark, brooding, and cynical but not always. If you go to Japan, the Hollow Ones there are mostly pink haired anime girls and brooding white haired pretty boys. It's a little silly to meet a bathrobe wearing Jedi mage with a functioning flashlight-saber but pop culture is the language they speak. It's no less dangerous too because they can still warp the fabric of reality with their mind. Mind you, a lot of them are in their late 30s now too and fairly potent.,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do they invade London at any point? </div> </div> </div>In the hypothetical Hellsing/WOD crossover, I imagine that Millennium is actually a Technocracy splinter group originally. The renegades leftover from when the Technocrat Allies and Traditionalists kicked their asses. They were always half-Nephandus anyway and the Freak Chip was made by their Progenitors branch. They planned to kill the Masquerade completely with their actions and probably did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-17-2019, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T17:50:33-08:00","id":1355533,"title":"","content":"<b>Malkavian Headcanon</b><br /> <br /> * The most common Malkavian derangements are as follows:<br /> <br /> 1. Paranoia<br /> 2. Guilt and self-loathing<br /> 3. Narcissism/Megalomania<br /> 4. An addiction of some kind (usually blood)<br /> 5. Poor impulse control (particularly anger)<br /> 6. Obsession with specific mortals or concepts (Gehenna)<br /> <br /> In other words, a good 50% of Malkavians are functionally identical to your typical Elder vampire in behavior.<br /> <br /> * Malkavians' Signature Discipline is not actually Dementation but Auspex. Many develop extra facility with it than other Kindred and it provides many of their uncanny &quot;insights&quot; that other vampires could have if they had less of a filter or more willingness to venture guesses based on what they discover.<br /> <br /> * A common Malkavian flaw is using Auspex all the time on everyone and everything or being unable to filter it when you touch people or objects.<br /> <br /> * While they never really reach Fishmalk status (that's an in-universe stereotype with no basis in reality), almost all Malkavians enjoy the occassional fucking with people.<br /> <br /> * Malkavian elders are every bit as obsessed with power as Toreador, Ventrue, and Tremere. They just prefer to use proxies, catspaws, and pawns. Many cities with a more &quot;traditional&quot; prince are actually under the control of a Malkavian.<br /> <br /> * Saulot was Malkav's brother. The two of them created the first Roads of Enlightenment.<br /> <br /> * There's a popular theory that Saulot WAS Malkav Pre-Golconda. There's an equally popular one that Malkav was Saulot Post-Golconda.<br /> <br /> * The Book of Nod was written by Malkav (allegedly).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T00:00:01-08:00","id":1355784,"title":"","content":"The vast majority of woks attributed to one ancient vampire or creature (such as the Book of Nod, the Erciyes Fragments, and so on) are faked. Caine, Lilith, the Second Generation and the Antedeluvians date from before written language and acquired vast and terrible powers before that innovation. They did not need it or have any reason to write things down. Many of the fakes are old, but an old fraud is still a fraud even if it is an antique in its own right.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T00:18:42-08:00","id":1355786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1355784#post1355784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The vast majority of woks attributed to one ancient vampire or creature (such as the Book of Nod, the Erciyes Fragments, and so on) are faked. Caine, Lilith, the Second Generation and the Antedeluvians date from before written language and acquired vast and terrible powers before that innovation. They did not need it or have any reason to write things down. Many of the fakes are old, but an old fraud is still a fraud even if it is an antique in its own right.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has always been my take on it as well. The idea of Caine writing a &quot;dear diary&quot; book never sat well with me. At best, some aspects of the BoN might have been oral stories handed down, things Caine told his childer and grandchilder, who in turn told others, who eventually wrote it down. But at that point, you're so far down the telephone game that the stories in the BoN must be anecdotal at best, tangentially related to the actual events at best. In my headcanon, the BoN, RotDM and EF are the kindred equivalent of creation myths and nothing more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T13:56:27-08:00","id":1355937,"title":"","content":"In BJD, Marcus Vitel manipulates Beckett by promising to give the Gangrel access to an ancient vampire text. It occurred to me when I read the book Vitel might have created the document 1800 years ago, and have been using it to trick people off and on over the centuries. Vampires are liars, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T15:25:43-08:00","id":1356180,"title":"","content":"<b>How I handle House Carna</b><br /> <br /> In my interpretation, House Carna is the beneficiary of a hurricane of good fortune and lucky accidents. She managed to get the Book of the Grave War that allows her to break the Blood Bonds and Dominate/Presence that kept her as well as many other Tremere mentally broken as well as enslaved to the Clan--possibly enslaving her to whatever Inconnu or Antediluvian who created the magical book (My suggestion would be the Master of Ravens).<br /> <br /> If Carna had done this rebellion at any other time in the Clan's history, they would have brought down the full force of the Camarilla on her and slaughtered all 20 or 30 Tremere vampires who she managed to win over to her side. However, it happened when Tremere had fled from Vienna and taken over Goratrix's body while Schrekt was preparing a plan against the Home Chantry that was now under the control of Kupala/Saulot/Whatever. In effect, she was unimportant and something that would have been dealt with later--probably by putting her on the Red List with a Tremere sponsorship. Poof. She's doomed.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, Tremere (the Antediluvian not the Clan) or whoever dismantled the defenses on Vienna and there was a massacre of the Council of Seven as well as burying of whatever was underneath the chantry under a thousand tons of rubble. House Carna suddenly found itself flooded with new recruits, maybe as many as two or three hundred and was now powerful enough to resist any encroachment on their territory. Worse, the Banu Haqim joined the Camarilla and the Tremere simply no longer had the JUICE to go after their renegade members. It didn't help Carna was now in a position to bargain Camarilla membership with the Inner Council for her and her girls even if House Schrekt (House Tremere) wanted them all destroyed.<br /> <br /> House Carna sits on a knife's edge as a result because it is a good alternative to the old Tremere and preaches freedom while not being Anarchs or Camarilla. However, Carna is a Low Humanity serial killer. Like if you put Elizabeth Bathory in charge of a House of Tremere. She's a ticking time bomb and Tremere the Ante is picking his own agents from the Tremere the Clan's remains to rebuild HIS house as House Goratrix (only nominally allied with the Sabbat now). Like the First Order in Star Wars.<br /> <br /> Will House Carna survive? Probably but its best bet to do that will be someone diablerizing her and taking over in her place like Erichtho or Maldavis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-20-2019, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T23:49:41-08:00","id":1356247,"title":"","content":"<b>Media and RL personas</b><br /> <br /> Almost all vampire media is unchanged in World of Darkness with the following changes.<br /> <br /> * All of the Anne Rice books have been adapted into films, like cheesy romance novels they show up every year.<br /> <br /> * Anne Rice's 20 year break from the Vampire Chronicles was due to being Dominated by the Prince of New Orleans into stopping. She resumed them when he was killed and the effect faded.<br /> <br /> * Sarah Michelle Gellar is stalked regularly by Brujah hecklers. Louis Fortier has had to stake a couple. One of them met the Final Death for his fandom of another series (see Revenant: The Weeping below).<br /> <br /> * Elvira, of all people, is one of the few horror actresses to actually be made into a vampire. The other notable one is Ingrid Pitt.<br /> <br /> * <i>Wes Cravens A New Nightmare</i> is a true story of what happened when he was stalked by a Bane. He donates heavily to the Arcanum each year.<br /> <br /> * Tim Burton is Sluagh Kinian. He films exactly what he sees.<br /> <br /> * Walt Disney was a NWO mage and Disneyland was actually built by the Technocracy. Oddly, he wasn't remotely sinister about any of it.<br /> <br /> * <i>Kindred: The Embraced</i>, which was called <i>Revenant: The Weeping</i>, was huge success. Aaron Spelling's take on beautiful immortal zombies lasted eight seasons as well as was a huge influence on <i>True Blood</i>, <i>Charmed</i>, and a few other vampire programs. The show was only cancelled when a Toreador superfan snuck in and attempted to turn two of the House Sukubi actresses.<br /> <br /> * <i>Revenant: Bloodthirst</i> was even more male gaze.<br /> <br /> * Peter Thiel is a Thin Blooded vampire. He can afford to drink the blood of children semi-publicly.<br /> <br /> * The real Elon Musk is a Son of Ether and in hiding with his identity assumed by a Progenitor Clone working for the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> * Quite a lot of the &quot;28 year curse&quot; members were Embraced by Toreador. So much so that it is now an order NOT to do it.<br /> <br /> * There's a much-much sleazier version of the Underworld series called WEREPOCALYPSE that includes copious nudity, gore, and an even more brainless plot. Pentex has produced many of these films.<br /> <br /> * Victor Temple replaces Suge Knight in music history with the House of Boom replacing Death Row records.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-21-2019, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T23:53:17-08:00","id":1356248,"title":"","content":"In my take, House Carna is composed entirely of Radical Feminist Nazis who wear pastel colored pleather (not leather) jackets with \u201cHouse Carna\u201d written on the back and tee-shirts with the slogan \u201cAsk me about my insubordination.\u201d Generally, the disappear into a crowd of vampires.<br /> <br /> They also like knocking around red pill types and MGTOW types and shoving them into school lockers.<br /> <br /> I kid.<br /> <br /> Mostly I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> assessment. However, I doubt the numbers get as high as 200, given there are not a lot of Tremere around in the first place. Also, Carna\u2019s might not be secretly enslaved to whomever made the \u201cBook of the Grave War\u201d because they might be dead. Yes, the Book is a tool of manipulation, but that only works if the creator is still alive and causing trouble.<br /> <br /> They rarely gather in large groups, but are converting existing members of clan Tremere around the world \u2013 and these Tremere do not announce their change in allegiance to the world at large, for the post part. A member of the local chantry might, or might not, be a subversive member of House Carna. It is so hard to tell and no one is really loyal to Tremere anymore.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T10:06:23-08:00","id":1356494,"title":"","content":"V5 Camarilla and V5 Anarch tells that two meetings happen, one with the Ministry with &quot;Justicars&quot; that went Boom! And other secretly with the Haqimites and The Tower parties to plot the explosion in the other meeting. If all Justicars from the five clans from the V20 to V5 are still around, there are some possibilities: 1) they were not Justicars, other parties posing as such, and they were good impersonators to foolish the Setite Elders into the trap. 2) they were actually Praetor Archons who the Camarilla sacrified. 3) They were Manuela the Brujah and/or Leigh the Gangrel with a bunch of archons. 4) The Justicars survived the explosion somehow. 5) Not a trap at all: The Second Inquisition was actually the cause of the explosion, and the Banu Haqim and the Camarilla sized the tragedy to form the Odense Pact.<br /> <br /> What happen and who really met final death at the first meeting and how?<br /> <br /> What do you thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24990,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24990-irad-the-strong","user":"Irad the Strong","date":". 12-22-2019, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24990-irad-the-strong","name":"Irad the Strong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24990_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T15:25:30-08:00","id":1356541,"title":"","content":"If we really want to justify it, I think Theo Bell was Dominated into killing ol'Hardy, which would be why the cam isn't making snuff films out of him. Still can't explain the Brujah leaving.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1356247#post1356247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> * Tim Burton is Sluagh Kinian. He films exactly what he sees.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is funny<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Walt Disney was a NWO mage and Disneyland was actually built by the Technocracy. Oddly, he wasn't remotely sinister about any of it. </div> </div> </div> What? Why?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * <i>Kindred: The Embraced</i>, which was called <i>Revenant: The Weeping</i>, was huge success. Aaron Spelling's take on beautiful immortal zombies lasted eight seasons as well as was a huge influence on <i>True Blood</i>, <i>Charmed</i>, and a few other vampire programs. The show was only cancelled when a Toreador superfan snuck in and attempted to turn two of the House Sukubi actresses. </div> </div> </div> I think you could work with kindred the embraced for a story, but this isn't how I'd do it. I'd say the reason why it sucked was because the vampiric producers really wanted to increase the inaccuracies to confuse hunters, not that Revenant was a particularly accurate series.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * <i>Revenant: Bloodthirst</i> was even more male gaze. </div> </div> </div> It was, in fact, a softcore porno game where you massacre the mentally ill, ethnic criminals, Asians and Christians, Also I prefer the title &quot;Revenant: Family Trees&quot; because it's closer/dumber.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * The real Elon Musk is a Son of Ether and in hiding with his identity assumed by a Progenitor Clone working for the Syndicate. </div> </div> </div> I feel you do him too much credit, and if Elon must be tied to a mage, he'd be a Technocrat, since he's promoting technocrat ideals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * There's a much-much sleazier version of the Underworld series called WEREPOCALYPSE that includes copious nudity, gore, and an even more brainless plot. Pentex has produced many of these films. </div> </div> </div> I don't know if this'd be better or worse. Curious thought; The Idea that Pentex increases the sex'n violence of their products lends credence to the Radio/TV/'videogames cause violence' shtick they're pulling, and their stake in the networks that follow that narrative... Well, I suppose the heads of the Hydra infight, but it's food for thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T16:14:55-08:00","id":1356544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1356541#post1356541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this'd be better or worse. Curious thought; The Idea that Pentex increases the sex'n violence of their products lends credence to the Radio/TV/'videogames cause violence' shtick they're pulling, and their stake in the networks that follow that narrative... Well, I suppose the heads of the Hydra infight, but it's food for thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>My view is that Pentex is on both ends of the scale. They simultaneously make the sleaziest, most exploitative trash they can (which does more damage to the actors and actresses than the viewer) and they also are the people who own the Radio Networks/Television Shows/Megachurches (which are corporations anyway) that talk about how awful as well as evil it all is. Pentex is the father of hypocrisy in culture after all.<br /> <br /> Weirdly, this is in 1984 where the Inner Party manufactures a lot of the illicit stuff the Proles consume while letting them think it's a rebellion against the party.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What? Why? </div> </div> </div>Weirdly, I kid you not, Los Angeles by Night said the Technocracy/NWO *DID* create Disneyland so it isn't headcanon at all. It was an experiment in controlling imagination.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It was, in fact, a softcore porno game where you massacre the mentally ill, ethnic criminals, Asians and Christians </div> </div> </div>So the game is identical? :rimshot:<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-22-2019, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T16:33:29-08:00","id":1356549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we really want to justify it, I think Theo Bell was Dominated into killing ol'Hardy, which would be why the cam isn't making snuff films out of him. Still can't explain the Brujah leaving.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take on the <b>Council of Prague</b> is the following (similar to my House Carna one):<br /> <br /> 1. [b]Theo Bell[/b was disgusted by the Inner Council throwing the Second Inqusition at the Anarchs and the Sabbat, especially since it's what caused the SI in the first place. Also, because the Anarchs helped fight the Sabbat in the East Coast Crusade as loyal allies as well as helped take New York. Throw in the fact that there's the fact the Camarilla was heavily involved in human trafficking in the Brujah Trilogy and he was all about killing Hardestadt.<br /> <br /> 2. What Theo Bell didn't count on was the fact that <b>Tyler</b> (a.k.a Patricia Bollingbrook) was at the location and saw her chance to eliminate Hardestadt as well. When Theo Bell took his shot, she used her power to raise the fury of the Brujah present and triggered a mass frenzy. Tensions were also especially high at the Council anyway because the usual shenanigans were going on behind the scenes anyway. Jan Pieterzoon and Lucinde had both planned to kill Hardestadt themselves with Bell as their suicide agent.<br /> <br /> 3. Jan ended up getting &quot;killed&quot; and Bell surviving due to the chaos and several Elders taking the opportunity to settle old scores. The complete breakdown of Kindred order was far worse than it should have been and either someone planned it beyond Tyler and Bell or the Beckoning had excarcebated everyone's mood to begin with. There were also some Anarchs present who helped Bell escape with some Archons too. Bell didn't kill Jan Pieterszoon and he's probably a prisoner in someone's dungeon right now or fleshcrafted to look like someone else (Lodin?) until they figure out what to do with him.<br /> <br /> 4. The exile of the Brujah is actually part of a larger Camarilla scheme that basically amounted to getting rid of what was termed to be useless Neonates. The Brujah Elders and Methuselahs were offered a place in the Camarilla as the Hellenites with hefty bribes while the assumption would be the Brujah Neonates/Rabble would get themselves purged in the Second Inquisition. The Caitiff would also be destroyed by it, removing the surplus population. While the Brujah lost their Inner Council member and Justicar, most Princes and so on didn't care. There was also the implicit promise that in a century or so they'd get this all back with the &quot;New Brujah&quot; taken from intellectual stock.<br /> <br /> 5. A lot of Brujah Elders DID defect, though, and took over the Anarchs to form their own sect on the ruins of the Sabbat's lost territory. Basically, they saw an opportunity to be the new big dogs over the Gangrel, Caitiff, House Ipsissimus, and vampires out of step with the Camarilla. The Ministry joining them meant that the Anarchs went from being a bunch of angry fools yelling at the wind into an opportunity for immense power over fools starving for leadership. The Brujah Elders probably wouldn't have done this if the Camarilla hadn't snubbed the Ministry.<br /> <br /> 6. Theo Bell has been spared the Red List in the chaos of this because the Camarilla is using him as a scapegoat. The threat of him being alive is enough that they'd prefer him alive at least for the next decade or so until this shakes out. Bell, himself, is in hiding--I don't care what the books say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-19-2020, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T17:21:33-08:00","id":1357137,"title":"","content":"Some mystical ones:<br /> <br /> * Mithras actually is a demigod who was the childe of a Sun Incarnae who was Embraced. This only adds to his enormous ego.<br /> <br /> * Similarly, so were the Gods of Egypt.<br /> <br /> * Apep is the Silent Strider name for the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> * Sutekh has no particular love for the Path of Typhon and considers it nothing more than an Apep cult that overtook the worship of his own faith that is more Anarchist philosophy.<br /> <br /> * Kemintiri is the founder of the Children of Osiris and it's nothing more than a tool for her to get revenge on the Followers of Set.<br /> <br /> * Keminitiri knows that the Followers of Set are hopelessly corrupted by the Cult of Apep but finds no reason to clarify what their founder would really want.<br /> <br /> * Apep worship was introduced to the Cult of Set by a Embraced 5th generation Silent Strider Abomination.<br /> <br /> * Set was slain by the entirety of the Silent Strider tribe working together. He is one of the few Antediluvians who is dead-dead.<br /> <br /> * Cappadocias is the ruler of a vast Far Shores realm which resembles Heaven and Hell that he takes the form of the Grim Reaper in.<br /> <br /> * Saulot allowed himself to die because he felt the Tremere would be needed as a weapon against the End Times, whatever they may be.<br /> <br /> * Kupala is the Worm inhabiting Tremere. It tried to take over Tzimisce but failed.<br /> <br /> * Tzimisce defeated Kupala by absorbing the minds of thousands of his fellow Tzimisce into one organism.<br /> <br /> * Lasombra allowed his physical body to be destroyed to become pure darkness. However, merging with hell may have destroyed it completely. What has replaced it may actually be worse.<br /> <br /> * The Cult of Shalim worships a creature in Hell that wishes to unmake reality, possibly Belial or a still-imprisoned Archdemon.<br /> <br /> * Antediluvians are immensely powerful beings but actually fairly small fish compared to the gods that are above and beyond Earth. They're more like Archmages or lesser Oracles than gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T17:34:13-08:00","id":1357140,"title":"","content":"Not strictly speaking V5, but...<br /> <br /> The Putanesca are among the most standup kindred out there. Sterling people. On the scale of kindred that is, not so much on the kine scale.<br /> <br /> Because in between the Giovanni curse, the kind of jobs the Giovanni throw them and the fact that the Giovanni just don't respect them enough to instruct them about paths, the unlife of a Putanesca from embrace to wighthood can be very, very short. Theres just very little room to manuver, morally. As a result, in my headcanon, the Putanesca have gotten more than a bit obsessive about their humanitas. The ones that don't hit wight in short order anyway, so a bit self-selecting there.<br /> <br /> In the modern nights, they could get instruction in paths from elsewhere, but by now the strong focus on humanitas in the bloodline is culturally ingrained.<br /> <br /> I also figure the Giovanni have taught them so little Necromancy that most don't find the discipline worth the effort. A few of them gather all the scraps they've been thrown and keep up the North American impression that they are great Necromancers, but most go for out-of-clans or overdevelop Dominate and Potence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T18:09:40-08:00","id":1357143,"title":"","content":"The Souleater theory is canon in V5. The Tzimisce (including their Anti) are a actually a huge Bane/Vampire hive mind and the Eater-of-Souls Wyrm's sleeper agent within the Kindred world. When the time (read: Apocalypse) comes, they will strike. Koldun is also a Talon of the Wyrm.<br /> The Ministry and the Baali may or may not serve the same purpose for the Defiler and Calamity Wyrm, respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T16:31:41-08:00","id":1357267,"title":"","content":"Part of the reason the Anarch movement seems so disorganized is...because it is. Anarch is actually a term the Camarilla applies to any Neonate or Ancilla who stands up against the existing power structures and the &quot;Movement&quot; quickly claims anyone who resists as one of their own whether they intend to be or not.<br /> <br /> One of the funniest moments of my campaign was when the PCs were being interrogated by a Justicar about the fact they'd had involvement in the death of a Prince and several Elders because he was a douchebag of La Croix proportions.<br /> <br /> Then they did a double take when they were referred to as, &quot;leading figures in the Anarch movement.&quot;<br /> <br /> They got even more confused when they met the local Anarchs in their new city and were feted as heroes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Wait, what?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T17:59:38-08:00","id":1357279,"title":"","content":"The Beckoning is a lie perpetrated by the inner circle to survive the second inquisition, really they and all the other influential elders are being ware housed under the Hague. The elders who refuse to play along are either black bagged or offered up to the 2nd =I= <br /> <br /> The sabbat are doing the same only in a series of underground cities lost to time (but not to the harbinger of skulls)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T18:52:29-08:00","id":1357283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1356247#post1356247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Almost all vampire media is unchanged in World of Darkness with the following changes.<br /> <br /> * All of the Anne Rice books have been adapted into films, like cheesy romance novels they show up every year.<br /> <br /> * Anne Rice's 20 year break from the Vampire Chronicles was due to being Dominated by the Prince of New Orleans into stopping. She resumed them when he was killed and the effect faded.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing in my chronicles, is that the big push to portray vampires as misunderstood lovers as opposed to brutal rapist-murderers is almost certainly pushed and supported by the Camarilla. They didn't start the trend, but once it became a thing, they jumped on board very quickly to support it.<br /> <br /> I typically don't use real celebrities and historical figures as people who interacted with vampires, but I do use roman-a-clef versions, and I'm totally going to use one for Anne Rice now. Good take and explanation. Of course, what you'll really need is &quot;Anne Rice&quot; as somehow having secret knowledge of real vampire society. Nothing as base as making her a ghoul, but perhaps a beloved pawn of some New Orleans Toreador who invites her to Elysium under his protection but variously presences her and dominates her into forgetting specifics, but which she &quot;remembers&quot; in dreams and uses as inspiration for her books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T12:38:33-08:00","id":1357383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1357137#post1357137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Antediluvians are immensely powerful beings but actually fairly small fish compared to the gods that are above and beyond Earth. They're more like Archmages or lesser Oracles than gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would have been a given since some of the Antes in Gehenna actually became something bigger and more powerful than what we'd expect from a high end vampire. Ennoia merging with the earth, Tzimisce and vissictude, Lasombra becoming an Oblivion beast or Cappadocious becoming a really powerful wraith all speak to a form of 'transcendance.' Indeed, that was one of the alternate stories - some Highlander-esque Vampire Gathering where they fought each other for the remains of power in an attempt to achieve what might be the vampiric equivalent of Ascension. So yeah, I'd totally see them as Archmages in the frame of 'Masters of the Art' because their high end disciplines (basically 'plot device') seem to fit in with that (nevermind Caine or the second generation.) Only the Vampires don't have paradox (they have other limitations) which in some ways makes them a bigger danger than an Archmage would be.<br /> <br /> Alternately, maybe you see the third generation (or other Methuselah) attempting to achieve some kind of transcendance only to become puppets/avatars of those 'more powerful, otherworld beings' - agents they can act through (if they aren't already.) Hell what if Golconda was a trick one such being used to gain such puppets (I could see a throwback to Trannsylvanian-chronicles 'Evil Saulot' with tha)<br /> <br /> This also has some interesting implications for the Baali and the Children, too.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1357143#post1357143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Souleater theory is canon in V5. The Tzimisce (including their Anti) are a actually a huge Bane/Vampire hive mind and the Eater-of-Souls Wyrm's sleeper agent within the Kindred world. When the time (read: Apocalypse) comes, they will strike. Koldun is also a Talon of the Wyrm.<br /> The Ministry and the Baali may or may not serve the same purpose for the Defiler and Calamity Wyrm, respectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the souleater concept, I just think the original incarnation felt too much like Vampire Flood. Less alien, more metaphysical horror. I think some ideas have tied Vissictude and the 'souleating' to Kupala, for example? If that wasn't enough you could even tie it to the Wyrm (or as close as VtM got to the Werewolf concept) as well. Or as above this might be something you could tie to the Children the Baali purportdly spoke of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1357279#post1357279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Beckoning is a lie perpetrated by the inner circle to survive the second inquisition, really they and all the other influential elders are being ware housed under the Hague. The elders who refuse to play along are either black bagged or offered up to the 2nd =I=<br /> <br /> The sabbat are doing the same only in a series of underground cities lost to time (but not to the harbinger of skulls)</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been thinking of the Beckoning as being the metaphyiscal pendulum shifting the other direction from the Time of Thin Blood and the withering. Things were dying out, but the world didn't end and now some power may be coming back, meaning the Antes - having been awakened - are now starting to flex their muscles and really get things started. That 'growing' power may have started towards the east (they always seemed to have more mystical mojo in that area of the world than in the West) and they've been marshalling resourcs to begin the next phase of Gehenna.<br /> <br /> Since I've also been interested in the Fractured Cosmos/Resonance idea I've been reading Ascension (and prepared to dig more into Demon) so the idea that perhaps the gauntlet and other barriers between the spiritual and material worlds are breaking down (we know the Giovanni wanted to do something like this, maybe other vampires were doing their own versions) so you could have the underworld, astral plane, etc. starting to flood back in (and all that metaphysical energy that was drying up suddenly floods back in.. literally).<br /> <br /> Until another turning point is reached, and something perhaps even worse happens. At that point I'm starting to think that the built up pressure of a flood of mystical energy might start tearing reality apart even more than it has (again that 'fractured cosmos/resonance' idea, only even worse) and you start getting REALLY apocalyptic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T18:40:27-08:00","id":1357433,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of bringing back this feeling of tense escalation toward something. The Y2K panic that Gehenna represented once is in the rear view mirror now, but the feeling of waiting for the other shoe to drop remains a part of the atmosphere in the real world's modern day.<br /> <br /> In a World of Darkness where Enoch was never hit with spirit nukes, whatever other forms of supernatural mayhem you have going on in modern Vampire, Mage, or Werewolf games could be the thing that leads to the first player-level Demons escaping the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T20:49:59-08:00","id":1357450,"title":"","content":"ANTEDILUVIAN HEADCANONS<br /> <br /> \u2022After leaving the Second City for good, Haqim departed eastward and after a period of exploration, chose the early settlements that would become Susa as the kine domain for him and his clan while the Zagros Mountains of the Persian Penninsula would fulfill the role of geographically defensible location for the security and concealment of what would become Alamut, hidden so deep within inaccessible sections the mountains that it would require kindred capabilities to reach.<br /> <br /> \u2022After the Second City, Ilyes and Troile would both participate in the founding of Troy as their combined masterwork, but later on as Ilyes grew more interested in broader politicking and other cities such as Athens, this became another one of the many tensions that would lead to Troile rising against her sire-lover.<br /> <br /> \u2022The Indus River Valley Civilization and its collapse was tightly connected to the falling out of the once lovers Ennoia and Ravnos and the horse-back nomads of Ennoia that eventually drove off Ravnos and his clan as they forced their chosen people eastward, beginning the long rivalry of Gangrel-Ravnos.<br /> <br /> \u2022[Lasombra] departed from the Second City filled with ambition and seeking both power and eternity. He departed to the Aegean where he would study certain Lilian and/or Wyrmish secrets that allowed him to begin channeling the Abyss while also being one of the stewards along with Akriel of the Neolithic Mediterranean. <br /> <br /> \u2022Saulot and The Eldest wandered together for a time, out into the Far East, traveling and studying philosophy for a time until a disagreement between the two antediluvians developing philosophies of trancendence caused them to part ways, but this travel has led both ancient's clans, although more prominently the Salubri, to have significant numbers throughout Asia.<br /> <br /> \u2022[Ventrue]'s disappearance has been explained via numerous rumors and fabrications over the millennia, yet all but a few vastly overstate the truth. The true reason that [Ventrue] departed the Second City was that the curse of Caine restricted his feeding to that of the First City and slowly the ancient's blood grew thin. While this issue may have been further aggravated by [Lasombra] or Troile striking out to weaken [Ventru] but the means for his disappearance was torpor as Caine naturally refused to revoke the curse, a large part of the reason for [Ventrue]'s pilgramage. They have risen for brief periods over the millennia but never for longer then a century due to their curse, yet always they have managed to shape the history of their clan and all kindred as only they can...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T21:01:42-08:00","id":1357451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1357450#post1357450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ANTEDILUVIAN HEADCANONS<br /> \u2022[Lasombra] departed from the Second City filled with ambition and seeking both power and eternity. He departed to the Aegean where he would study certain Lilian and/or Wyrmish secrets that allowed him to begin channeling the Abyss while also being one of the stewards along with Akriel of the Neolithic Mediterranean.</div> </div> </div> </div>On my end?<br /> <br /> Dispater, Patron Demon of the Giovanni, is actually Lasombra. Hence why them having Oblivion is actually not that strange at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1357450#post1357450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022After the Second City, Ilyes and Troile would both participate in the founding of Troy as their combined masterwork, but later on as Ilyes grew more interested in broader politicking and other cities such as Athens, this became another one of the many tensions that would lead to Troile rising against her sire-lover.</div> </div> </div> </div>One fun thing I play with is the idea that Ilyes IS Ventrue and Troile was a 4th generation vampire who slew Ventrue then became an Antediluvian herself.<br /> <br /> A few more Troile and Carthage headcanon.<br /> <br /> * Troile and Moloch were both believers they had to keep the Children acquiesced to SAVE THE WORLD.<br /> <br /> * Menele is in complete historical revision mode about what a festering shithole Carthage became.<br /> <br /> * Helena was actually driven away from it because of the Baali infestation.<br /> <br /> * The Trujah are all descended from Troile but their own bloodline. They severed their emotions to cut themselves off from the Baali's taint. It also severed them from the timeline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-29-2019, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T23:23:13-08:00","id":1357463,"title":"","content":"[RE: Lasombra]<br /> \u2022Neat, I'll have to check out the Giovanni books a bit to brush up on Dispater. I hadn't known about Oblivion as the discipline although personally I think the distinction between Necromancy &amp; Obtenebration served both clans and their thematics well and some syncretism of them would be doing a disservice, although that's an edition debate tangent.<br /> <br /> [RE: Brujah]<br /> \u2022That is a neat way of reading the distinction between Ilyes &amp; Troile and syncretizing it with Ventru's fate. Naturally it's distinct from my HC but I can definitely see it's merits, but I'm gonna slip this into my back pocket as an OOC alternative for myself and IC rumor.<br /> <br /> -I can definitely see that theology being the kind that could have been sympathetic to Troile, even at its worst, few of the antediluvians ever struck me as the infernalist type. Even The Eldest had a work-around of sorts.<br /> <br /> -I'm not familiar with Chicago by Night, Helene, or Menele so I can't speak to that. I should probably look it up at some point.<br /> <br /> -That's another solid HC that I'll probably back pocket it as well, as it is a neat idea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T23:38:08-08:00","id":1357466,"title":"","content":"I could see Lasombra having infernalist leanings, with creeps like the Angellis Ater being more like their clan founder than anyone outside the clan suspects, but that only works for me as an option because the Abyss was revealed to be the prison of the Fallen at such a late date in the history of White Wolf's publishing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T23:38:22-08:00","id":1357467,"title":"","content":"Lasombra, Hecate and at least one branch of the Baali are draw their power from the Neverborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T00:20:05-08:00","id":1357475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1357466#post1357466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see Lasombra having infernalist leanings, with creeps like the Angellis Ater being more like their clan founder than anyone outside the clan suspects, but that only works for me as an option because the Abyss was revealed to be the prison of the Fallen at such a late date in the history of White Wolf's publishing.</div> </div> </div> </div>One idea is that Lasombra was eventually replaced by a demon of the Slayers [Underworld] or Defilers [Ocean] House and he's a meat suit for a Neverborn/Fallen.<br /> <br /> It's just this Neverborn wants to plunge the world into Eternal Darkness for an Exalted-esque plan.<br /> <br /> Unlike most Fallen, it doesn't want to DESTROY creation to END it but that Creation will merge with the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Once everyone is dead and the world is united with the Shadowlands (see Augustus Giovanni), Lasombra and his demonic patron can rebuild it as a Paradise of Darkness.<br /> <br /> It's utterly insane--except, as in Exalted, entirely possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T03:35:11-08:00","id":1357499,"title":"","content":"Personally, if I had to canonize any kind of Kindred of the East timeline, I would do it like this:<br /> <br /> <b>How I did the Wan Kuei Invasion in my campaign</b><br /> <br /> <i>Note: I hate the Great Leap Outward as a name and will never use it.</i><br /> <br /> The Wan Kuei have their own version of the War of the Ages and with the rising tide of population in the world, more humans were turning into new Kuei Jin than the older ones could control them. Thus, the Chinese Wan Kuei came up with a perfectly devious and evil plan of getting their rebellious Communist and Capitalist childer out of their hair. They decided to do as Henry IV and busy giddy minds in foreign quarrels.<br /> <br /> The plan basically consisted of using a bunch of rabble rousers to create a populist racist war against the Kindred of the West. All manner of slander, libel, and accusations were directed at the Cainites (some of which was true). They gave the younger vampires a ticket, told them to go invade California, and kill the Foreign Devils who were hideous monsters every bit as evil as the Yama Kings.<br /> <br /> This, of course, was all bullshit but a surprisingly effective bullshit that worked just fine from the Wan Kuei's perspective. Fighting against the Anarchs eliminated a lot of their extraneous childer and didn't have a likelihood of causing problems for the Wan Kuei at home because the Free States didn't have a way of retaliating against their Chinese enemies. Hell, they barely understood they existed let alone their strains of influence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Camarilla and Jade Courts had a few meetings after the initial assumed this was a full-scale invasion. Several large cash payments, exchange of stolen relics, and negotiation via the Tremere in Hong Kong resulted in roughly this being communicated:<br /> <br /> &quot;No, we're just going after the Anarchs in California.&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, well, that's fine.&quot;<br /> &quot;We know you'll try to take it back.&quot;<br /> &quot;True but we'll let you murder the Anarchs first.&quot;<br /> &quot;Wouldn't have it any other way.&quot;<br /> <br /> Notably, La Croix was selected as an expendable Prince by Lucinde for this exact reason. </div> </div> </div>There were a few higher-ranking Wan Kuei among the invaders but generally, they were like Ming Xiao and had managed to tick off people back in the homeland that this was a kind of exile. Much blood was spilled and it looked like the Anarch Free States would collapse. However, time eventually turned against them.<br /> <br /> In simple terms, the Wan Kuei have no real gain from holding territory in California since they don't appear there naturally. They can feed on the humans there but domain isn't really as big a deal there since many can feed easier than Cainites. They also weren't going to be getting any of the wealth or power of the Cainites they slew since most Anarchs didn't have either. In the end, the Wan Kuei gradually lost of a war of attrition against the Anarchs. The Camarilla managed to briefly step in with La Croix but the death of both he and Ming Xiao resulted in the Anarchs retaking LA.<br /> <br /> They were, to use a colloquialism, a paper tiger.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It was also thoroughly unnecessary too since the elimination of the Ravnos Clan also meant there was plenty of new territory to feed opening up in India, though the local Immortals weren't inclined to let bygones be bygones there either. </div> </div> </div>Anyway, the joke may be on the Jade Courts and Camarilla both as it eventually happened that the surviving invaders finally did stop to talk with the Anarchs after years of brutal warfare. It didn't take much to convince the soldiers on the ground that they'd been had. Mostly because you had to be an idiot not to see the writing on the wall when reinforcements were requested, only to get the response, &quot;Sorry, not our problem&quot; and their passports back to their homeland revoked.<br /> <br /> The Dance of the Thrashing Dragon and the Anarch Iconoclasts have since come to a bit of an agreement to leave each other alone. They have also cooperated more than any of the Elders of either the Jade Courts or Camarilla would have expected. In simple terms, following the collapse of the New Promise Mandarite, plenty of Wan Kuei gangs now exist in the Anarch Free States indistinguishable from typical Anarch Baronies.<br /> <br /> How did the Anarch Free States rebuild itself to full power in less than 20 years? Not just the fact Anarchs Embrace faster but the fact Thin Bloods and Wan Kuei are supporting the dream. Someday the Wan Kuei of California may repay their elders for their betrayal but right now, making sure any who try to establish business in California suffer is enough.<br /> <br /> Oh and perhaps helping their friends in Hong Kong who resist the Jade Courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-29-2019, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T03:58:13-08:00","id":1357502,"title":"","content":"<b>Dastur Anosh</b> is the <b><i>Assamite Antitribu </i></b>who created the <b>Path of Caine </b>(why he has a 9 in it) as a corruption of the <b>Path of Blood </b>to teach to their Sabbat allies almost as a joke. As the Get of Khayyin are inferior and corrupt creatures who can never follow the &quot;true&quot; Assamite way, they couldn't be taught the Path of Blood. So he basically filed the serial numbers off and passed off its diablerie worship and so on to worship Caine instead despite the Path of Blood being created to kill Caine's childer.<br /> <br /> At least the <i>Web of Knives</i> version.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's when Dastur Anosh found out....SOMETHING in his studies of the Cult of Zillah and the True Hand as well as the Baali. Whatever he discovered resulted in him repudiating the Path of Blood and being horribly disgusted with Ur-Shulgi as well as all of the Assamite Antitribu that chose to go back to Alamut to follow him Most likely that Ur-Shulgi, Father of the Road of Blood, is the third Baali. Also that virtually everything they know about Haqim is probably bullshit since Zillah seems to have been someone who Embraced Haqim rather than Haqim claiming his own Embrace.<br /> <br /> Dastur had been more or less using the Path of Caine as a substitute for the Path of Blood simply by rote repetition for centuries by that point anyway so he's now clinging to it even though he knows its a fake religion (as he created it). He has thus deluded himself into believing a very different history about himself and now sincerely believes in his cult.<br /> <br /> Because without it, what has he?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T11:52:24-08:00","id":1357583,"title":"","content":"There is a small Bloodline of sane Malkavians. Malkav supposedly slew all his childer who did not descend into madness post curse from Caine. A few escaped. The bloodline survives by pretending to be Ventrue. These individuals are able to access the madness network but at a price. <br /> <br /> Malkav's childer killed Malkav. <br /> <br /> Ventrue escaped death via Astral projection. Ventrue lives by possessing other kindred, hopping from one body to the next.<br /> <br /> Malkav's twin, Malakai, is his madness made manifest. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T20:58:37-08:00","id":1357672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1357583#post1357583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a small Bloodline of sane Malkavians. Malkav supposedly slew all his childer who did not descend into madness post curse from Caine. A few escaped. The bloodline survives by pretending to be Ventrue. These individuals are able to access the madness network but at a price.<br /> <br /> Malkav's childer killed Malkav.<br /> <br /> Ventrue escaped death via Astral projection. Ventrue lives by possessing other kindred, hopping from one body to the next.<br /> <br /> Malkav's twin, Malakai, is his madness made manifest.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You could also have all of Malkav's childer having diablerized him together, so that's why he's in all of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T21:01:27-08:00","id":1357673,"title":"","content":"<i>A tuna walks into a sushi bar and tells the chef, &quot;You killed my father!&quot;</i><br /> <i>Chef says &quot;That's my business, fish.&quot;</i><br /> <i>The tuna thinks this for a moment and says &quot;Very well. Then I challenge you to a game of chess. If I win, you stop being a chef forever.&quot;</i><br /> <i>&quot;And if I win?&quot; asks the chef.</i><br /> <i>&quot;Then you can feed me to your customers,&quot; says the tuna.</i><br /> <i>So they start to play. Now, tunas love to play chess so in a few moves the tuna has the chef checkmated.</i><br /> <i>&quot;Looks like I win,&quot; says the tuna.</i><br /> <i>The chef nods and plunges his knife into the tuna's belly.<br /> &quot;</i><i>But I won!&quot; says the tuna.</i><br /> <i>&quot;So did you father,&quot; says the chef.<br /> <br /> ====</i><br /> <br /> This is not actually a random bit of wackiness but the Malkavian Madness Network warning the PC in Bloodlines against siding with La Croix. La Croix has murdered the PC's sire and the player character is playing a game of chess with him. The thing the PC needs to understand is that La Croix is going to murder them no matter what they do, just like La Croix murdered their sire. You should not expect the unjust and corrupt to abide by rules and if you abide by the rules with them, you will get screwed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-30-2019, 01:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T22:39:59-08:00","id":1357687,"title":"","content":"Solid advice in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T09:28:38-08:00","id":1357799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1357583#post1357583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ventrue escaped death via Astral projection. Ventrue lives by possessing other kindred, hopping from one body to the next.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Ventrue stepped into the Astral Plane... and vanished. He woke to find himself trapped in the past, facing mirror images that were not his own, and driven by an unknown force to change vampiric history for the better. His only guide on this journey is a spirit, an comrade from his own time, who appears in the form of a illusion that only Ventrue can see and hear. And so Ventrue finds himself leaping from unlife to unlife, striving to put right what once went wrong, and hoping each time that his next leap, will be the leap home...&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T09:36:26-08:00","id":1357802,"title":"","content":"Bloodlines had a lot of problems, but I really feel like LaCroix wasn't qualified to be Ventrue, Let alone a prince. Though I think, genuinely, If you played your cards right, and the Sarcophagus wasn't so dangerous, he would've given up on trying to dispose of you, and would've been all carrot from there on; Individualy by that point in the game you were a one-vampire army and would've made too many friends (or too many people owe you). If you could actually acquire useful ghouls and a defensible haven, you'd have been solid. Perhaps a primogen or on equal footing to LaCroix (assuming he didn't eat some ancient) <br /> <br /> I of course, never sided with him, that'd be stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T12:17:53-08:00","id":1357854,"title":"","content":"[Regional Age Variance]<br /> Vampires, Cainites specifically, can be mapped to a certain extent by following their expansion. Their are exceptions to these rules as clans such as the Gangrel, Malkavians, Nosferatu, Ravnos, &amp; Lasombra (where sea travel could be involved) have spread to basically wherever humanity was, throughout prehistory. Throughout the Neolithic there were Ravnos amongst Kuei-Jin, Malkavians amongst the Laibon, and Nosferatu amongst the Drowned Legacies; etc.<br /> <br /> That aside, let's break it down somewhat:<br /> <br /> \u2022The Middle East: Mesopotamia, Egypt, The Levant, The Iranian Penninsula, the Caucuses, etc. The Fertile Crescent was the womb of human civilization and it is almost certainly where Enoch and the Second City were located. (Some kindred claim Enoch was Ubar... perhaps Ubar was the title of the Second City?). Within the Middle East, you'll find some of the oldest kindred in the world. Methuselahs sleep beneath elder cities which they ruled 5,000 years ago and the blood of ancients is strong here. Noddists who have ventured here know, that while the appearances of modernity and today's struggle may disguise it, there is no better argument for the truth of Nod then to venture into this ancient land. The land where history walks and myths grow hungry...<br /> <br /> \u2022Beyond The Middle East, we have the next general ring of growth which has essentially two phases imo. First you have the dispersal after the Fall of the Second City, the Baali Wars, and those exiled or given to wandering. These reached the Mediterranean, Europe, North Africa, and Asia. While they were spread loosely at first, the second phase (perhaps caused by the Bronze Age Collapse and transition into the Iron Age) would see kindred fill out Europe (including its north and islands), North Africa (down to the Sahara and those few willing to venture below where traveling clans had long reached in Sub-Saharan Africa), and filling out the kindred populations of East Asia, where kindred society would develop particular distinctions over the millennia due to sheer distance from the relatively connected Near East, Europe, and Northern Africa. These became the land of younger methuselahs (a phrase with horrifying implications) and true elders. These lands developed into the cultures and states that are the recognizable predesccors of the nation's that we would come to know today. This is where the Jyhad truly came into its own, now spanning continents with its plots and tactics as 13 clans battled with the direction of now primordial ancients. Kindred here are entrenched and time moves slowly for the kindred. Nearly two millennia passed and much of it began to look the same for the elders to stand above it all. Little could shake these settled lands. Until, finally, humanity rose up with the fires of Inquisition...<br /> <br /> \u2022The New Worlds <br /> -The Americas and Australia cannot be understated in the history of the Jyhad. After over ten millennia in the Middle East and almost half that time in the Old World, the kindred had grown so incredibly static and fossilized that time may as well have become still for those who could see above the petty drama of specific cities and dynasties. The New World changed the scope. Both for the machinations of ancient and elder as well as for the young and desperate who chafed the yoke of the Old Powers. Kindred accompanied the first colonists of the colonial period with a hunger that rivaled that of the imperialists. These first kindred, largely young turks who were both hungry and disposable became the vassal waves of the old powers and while they carried ancient interests, they also began new ones. Young kindred could strive for domain and power while ancients knew the chessboard. It truly was a land of opportunity for vampires and given the relative time scale of cainites, with less then a millennia under their belts, the land of the new worlds remain the turbulent domains of young powers and young dynasties that can still battle in heated contests for supremacy and control.<br /> -[Due to the dangers of travel and the tendency of old kindred to remain within their long won domains, I have vanishingly few old world elders and even fewer methuselahs in the new world in my setting. Reading canon WW it felt like any B+ city had a half dozen true elders and maybe a methuselahs to its name, which struck me as both ridiculous and needlessly limiting, not to mention undermining the thematic divide between New and Old Worlds. This is why in my own setting, while old world backrooms and conspiracies may have shaped the new world, relatively young kindred are the authors of vampiric domains and legacies throughout the new world.]<br /> <br /> [Break Down]<br /> \u2022Tier One: The Middle East (Ancients &amp; Old Methuselahs)<br /> \u2022Tier Two: Old World (Methuselahs &amp; True Elders<br /> \u2022Tier Three: New World (Young Elders &amp; Ancillae)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T16:04:21-08:00","id":1358721,"title":"","content":"Things I do in my games that are just background:<br /> <br /> <b>Masquerade Headcanon</b><br /> <br /> * Serial killers are viewed as far more common than in RL and is a thing that regularly happens.<br /> * Occult-style murder hysteria is still believed in because, well, it's true in the World of Darkness. It's like shootings sadly in that it's a real thing that people tune out on the news.<br /> * Organized crime is still a major thing in the United States and functions like it does in certain countries as an untouchable pillar. When a house full of bodies is found, people assume it's an organized crime disposal site.<br /> * Due to the deteriorating situation in the world, protests and riots are actually more common. This is often stirred up by the Camarilla and Sabbat to cover up their activities but happens naturally.<br /> * There's every bit as much conspiracy theory as there is in RL. Anti-vaxxers, UFOs, lizard people, pedophile conspiracies, and government black ops. The thing is, these are ALL WRONG but they misinterpret the real evidence for other conspiracies. So, the irony is that the real stuff going on is obfuscated by layers and layers of weird.<br /> * There are thousands of experts who know the truth. Probably tens of thousands actually. The thing is that people who know about the supernatural and believe get recruited into one of the groups adjacent to it. If you're not killed, mind-wiped, or too scared to hide then you're likely to be a secretary for the Technocracy or an Arcanum professor.<br /> * People do believe in the supernatural a lot more than they do in the quote-unquote real world. It's just there's every bit as much bullshit if not more than in the real world. Fortune tellers, astrology, occult stores, Wellness, crystals, and so on are in every phone book. Finding the real stuff is almost impossible.<br /> * Horror practical special effects never went out of style. That combined with CGI means there's always massive numbers of Youtube videos of fake horrible murders because that's just a thing do. Interspersed between them is the occasional RL snuff film.<br /> * Cellphone jammers are a real thing that a lot of vampires carry around and other supernaturals. There's also an enhanced version that prevents video and pictures from being taken.<br /> * Police are just X more corrupt in the world. The New York City level of corruption never went away because it serves Camarilla interests and is just how police do business (many countries are this way anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-03-2020, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T06:41:06-08:00","id":1358853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1358721#post1358721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Masquerade Headcanon</b><br /> <br /> * There's every bit as much conspiracy theory as there is in RL. Anti-vaxxers, UFOs, lizard people, pedophile conspiracies, and government black ops. The thing is, these are ALL WRONG but they misinterpret the real evidence for other conspiracies. So, the irony is that the real stuff going on is obfuscated by layers and layers of weird..</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but this is terribly, terribly WRONG. <br /> Pentex are OF COURSE putting some terrible shit in their vaccinations, UFOs are just Etherites trying to get people to believe. Lizard people exist as some breed of formor if we don't want to bring mokoles into things, pedophiles are rampant (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westminster_paedophile_dossier\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westmi...ophile_dossier</a>), and the CIA is of course responsible for literally every problem south of the border<br /> <br /> Fuck; the CIA probably hires First teams. Isn't it amazing how a country with such a military industrial complex (The US) has such an unstable neighbour (Mexico) and yet seeks to solve problems in... Iran? Well of course if latin america was cleaned up how would the US have a drug problem? How is the CIA not directly wyrm influenced? <br /> <br /> In the WoD, every conspiracy theory, even the ones we wouldn't like to be true because of our politics, has a greater degree of justification for their formation (supernaturals making everything worse). This especially annoyed me in v5 with the little section on &quot;LoL lizard people are silly&quot; in a fucking book about literal vampires who've infiltrated and abused society. Might as well wrote &quot;All right-wing beliefs are entirely unfounded but all left-wing beliefs are true&quot; /Smug (I mean, yeah, right wing <i>conspiracies</i> are largely pretty unfounded<i> in the real world</i>, but pay attention to the fucking context you're writing in you daft fool) <br /> <br /> All the conspiracy theories are either entirely true or a misinterpretation of a real conspiracy. All of them. There's nothing there that's a 100% false.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T06:46:19-08:00","id":1358854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1358853#post1358853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the conspiracy theories are either entirely true or a misinterpretation of a real conspiracy. All of them. There's nothing there that's a 100% false.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even the pizza pedophiles?<br /> <br /> :gasp:<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T08:00:40-08:00","id":1358861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1357854#post1357854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Regional Age Variance]<br /> Vampires, Cainites specifically, can be mapped to a certain extent by following their expansion...</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally follow this sort of rule as well. In the materials I am developing for my games, I repeatedly point out that vampires who are considered &quot;elders' in cities like San Francisco or Denver or even Boston are often nothing but glorified ancillae when they visit cities like Rome, Byzantium, Jerusalem, or Baghdad. And if you want to be a Prince at the tender age of 350.... head west, my son. But vampires have a resistance to moving... it used to be extremely dangerous, and it is still fraught with peril.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T08:02:37-08:00","id":1358862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legendre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1358861#post1358861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I generally follow this sort of rule as well. In the materials I am developing for my games, I repeatedly point out that vampires who are considered &quot;elders' in cities like San Francisco or Denver or even Boston are often nothing but glorified ancillae when they visit cities like Rome, Byzantium, Jerusalem, or Baghdad. And if you want to be a Prince at the tender age of 350.... head west, my son. But vampires have a resistance to moving... it used to be extremely dangerous, and it is still fraught with peril.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a different view on this and I admit it reflects my Drowned Legacies alternative.<br /> <br /> &quot;When the Ventrue, Toreador, Brujah, and more came to South America, they found...a bunch of Ventrue, Toreador, Brujah, and more. They were just going by different names.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T08:14:01-08:00","id":1358866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1358854#post1358854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even the pizza pedophiles?<br /> <br /> :gasp:</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's just the Seventh Generation doing their thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member",