book/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T08:21:31-08:00","id":1358871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1358870#post1358870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember how I used to laugh at the disgusting idea of a bunch of rich celebrities serving the Wyrm with a pedophile ring. I wonder now if it was based on Epstein.<br /> <br /> Presumably he and the other implicated celebrities were just straight up members in the WOD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Friendly reminder that Jeffrey Epstein didn't kill himself. He just escaped to the Deep Umbra.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T08:27:25-08:00","id":1358873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1358871#post1358871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Friendly reminder that Jeffrey Epstein didn't kill himself. He just escaped to the Deep Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where he was killed by a party of Childling Pooka.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T08:31:41-08:00","id":1358876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1358874#post1358874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if the Baali, with their mystery origins and vague creation myth(s), are feeling the Beckoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>One bit of headcanon I have is the Baali are like....15 total in the world. There's Mary the Black, the Founders, and maybe a dozen others spread out. They're not a vast sinister conspiracy because, ironically, they succeeded in their mission.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat are the inheritors of all their Satanic rites and messy demon-worship.<br /> <br /> It's just the average Sabbat has no idea WHAT they're doing or WHY but go through the motions anyway.<br /> <br /> Another bit of headcanon is that the Baali are 99% percent sure that the rites they do to keep the Children asleep/awaken the Children are working. The remaining 1% is both sides worry they do the exact opposite or have no effect at all since they're not actually the geniuses at understanding demonology they think they are.<br /> <br /> Which makes the Baali even scarier when you realize they know about as much about their patrons as the average Cthulhu cultist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T09:33:00-08:00","id":1358889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1358862#post1358862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a different view on this and I admit it reflects my Drowned Legacies alternative.<br /> <br /> &quot;When the Ventrue, Toreador, Brujah, and more came to South America, they found...a bunch of Ventrue, Toreador, Brujah, and more. They were just going by different names.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The only &quot;native&quot; new world vampires in my game are the Brujah, and they are only &quot;native&quot; because a Brujah named The Wearer of Thunder fled the destruction of Carthage by travellng through the Borderlands of the spirit world to escape. (Brujah in my games have Necromancy, which is one of the reasons that they have the name &quot;Brujah&quot;.) He popped up in the Mayan kingdoms, and was ultimately the reason that they abandoned their cities and moved down into the lowlands. So there were a bunch of Aztec and Mayan Brujah when the first vampires (Lasombra, as it happens) showed up with the Spanish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T10:34:05-08:00","id":1358897,"title":"","content":"Vampires, like humans and lupines, spread to near every continent before the dawn of writing. Because of lupines and their ilk, vampires suffered tremendously in Northern America and Australia, where there wasn't enough humans to hide among. Among other reasons, the clans that could hide well and do well with less people, such as the Gangrel, Nosferatu, Ravnos, Lasombra and, curiously, the Settites managed to survive in these regions, but the Brujah, Ventrue, Toreador and Tzmisce didn't stand a chance. <br /> <br /> For southern America, obviously, the latter clans could do well; There were cities for them, sometimes even temples dedicated to them. Of course, the European vampires did not like this one bit, and were overwhelmingly successful in wiping out the local competition. To this day the Europeans are searching for aboriginal ancients to devour in South America, dreading the time they may wake up and reclaim their lands.<br /> <br /> If there were ever vampires on Australia before colonization, they were especially terrifying. Sparse food and plenty of changing breeds is not a good environment for vampires, and the bushfires, while not nearly as bad as now... An aboriginal elder of Australia's gotta be on the same level as a methuselah anywhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T11:35:08-08:00","id":1358907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1358876#post1358876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One bit of headcanon I have is the Baali are like....15 total in the world. There's Mary the Black, the Founders, and maybe a dozen others spread out. They're not a vast sinister conspiracy because, ironically, they succeeded in their mission.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ages ago - like in the late 1990s - I did a spread sheet with a rough estimate on the numbers of vampires in clans and bloodlines. Most bloodlines should have fewer than 50 members. So 15 Baali checks out, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T11:53:38-08:00","id":1358912,"title":"","content":"I think the opposite<br /> <br /> There are way more infernalists and Baali than you'd be lead to believe. <br /> It's just that the vast majority keep their heads down and don't bother with the whole -sell yourself to demons- kinda thing, or that -let's do atrocities to satiate the demons- nonsense. They just act like other clans. A huge number of baali were absorbed by House Tremere during the omen wars. Oh, they're a clan, not a bloodline, but obviously they don't advertise and are loath to give the impression that there's more of them. You've all been successfully duped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T12:01:54-08:00","id":1358915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1358912#post1358912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the opposite<br /> <br /> There are way more infernalists and Baali than you'd be lead to believe.<br /> It's just that the vast majority keep their heads down and don't bother with the whole -sell yourself to demons- kinda thing, or that -let's do atrocities to satiate the demons- nonsense. They just act like other clans. A huge number of baali were absorbed by House Tremere during the omen wars. Oh, they're a clan, not a bloodline, but obviously they don't advertise and are loath to give the impression that there's more of them. You've all been successfully duped.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on how you want to play them. Are they the ultimate threat to reality? The creeping hidden horror the Assamites still fear?<br /> <br /> Or are, in reality, the average demon-worshiping monster ready to corrupt your soul is....a Setite?<br /> <br /> Mind you, if the Tremere did have a Baali problem, it puts a new spin on the Fall of Vienna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T13:45:12-08:00","id":1358925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1358912#post1358912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, they're a clan, not a bloodline, but obviously they don't advertise and are loath to give the impression that there's more of them. You've all been successfully duped.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that too. The whole Saulot/Cappadocius/Eldest origin myth is a red herring. Ashur/The Slave Boy was probably a Nephandus or Fomor child (or even a surviving Nephilim) embraced by a 2nd gen as a curiosity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T14:24:46-08:00","id":1358933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1358915#post1358915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or are, in reality, the average demon-worshiping monster ready to corrupt your soul is....a Setite?</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me of something I noticed way forever ago that upset me about every Baali origin not pointing the finger right at Set; Other than their trademark special disciplines, the Baali and Setites have the same disc spread. Both have a heavy dose of &quot;corrupt the everyones&quot; vibe. Both have weaknesses that take a traditional vamp bane and double down on that bane. And I'm <i><b>not </b></i>supposed to believe the Baali are just an offshoot of Setites?! Please. The FoS clearly just picked a single dark evil figurehead to worship, while the Baali are more polytheistic about the whole thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T04:10:24-08:00","id":1359041,"title":"","content":"The Tremere don't have a problem with Baali.... Not a problem at all. <br /> <br /> But as for the Set/Baali connection; there's A LOT of clans and bloodlines with the same disciplines bar their one special. Lasombra/Giovanni, Assamite warrior/Street gangrel, Gargoyle/Lamia/Blood brother. Salubri/Cappadocian. Disciplines are altered by what a vampire lineage does, not because they've all got the same founder who decided on a whim to give his childer something different this time. The Settites and the Baali just happen to both like secretive cults, so they've developed the best two disciplines for that alongside their special one. <br /> <br /> Also I'm rather fond of their philosophical points. I do wish the books highlighted this more. Every time a Settite is used as a demon's thrall because someone can't tell the difference on how they were supposed to be run... I mean, I get it, Demons are sexy, Snake cults are sexy; there's nothing wrong with that pulpy goodness; but my cerebrum screams at me when I see people wanting to blur the two and have infernal settites the <i>set</i> default.. I get that, y'know, Stalin's Soviet Union and Nazi Germany had a lot in common to the point that at a basic glance you can't tell the difference, but they fought eachother for reasons beyond the need to have an external enemy (Though that was mostly it) <br /> <br /> My Followers of Set are all about breaking those chains (With a lot of hypocrisy) They're Libertarians (The &quot;don't tread on me&quot; Snake was not a coincidence) if you can ignore the cult-controlling hierachies and isolation (Let's not pretend Libertarians don't have a contradictory ideology) <br /> My Baali cults are all about serving or mastering demons (With a lot of Hypocrisy.) They're facists; they like the idea of coming together under a strong hierarchical system. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T13:05:00-08:00","id":1359113,"title":"","content":"I am inclined to agree with the idea that there are not many Baali by blood, but they probably exercise an outsize influence owing to the number of infernalists (from other clans and bloodlines) they control or at least manipulate.<br /> <br /> Edit: And some of the Baali worship Cthulhu-type creatures rather than traditional demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 01-05-2020, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T13:13:06-08:00","id":1359118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1359113#post1359113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am inclined to agree with the idea that there are not many Baali by blood, but they probably exercise an outsize influence owing to the number of infernalists (from other clans and bloodlines) they control or at least manipulate.<br /> <br /> Edit: And some of the Baali worship Cthulhu-type creatures rather than traditional demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the word Demon outside of The Fallen tends to cover a large variety of icky beings. It's the 'here be dragon's' catch all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25877-mithras304","name":"Mithras304","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25877_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T06:35:51-08:00","id":1359268,"title":"","content":"<b>Baali</b><br /> <br /> * The Baali are effectively wiped out and have been for millennium. Carthage was their last heyday and after Carthage, the ones in the Middle Ages were eventually smashed as well. They remain a Kindred boogeyman, though, because that allows other Kindred to believe they're at least not as bad as THOSE guys.<br /> <br /> <b>Sabbat</b><br /> <br /> * Polonia is technically Regent of the Sabbat but has long since lost control over the Gehenna War and is terrified of what he's unleashed. Unfortunately, there's no chance he'll ever be accepted among the defecting Sabbat so he must ride this dragon until the very end.<br /> <br /> <b>Anarchs</b><br /> <br /> * <b>The Ministry</b> fully expected to find a bunch of drooling morons when they joined the Movement. They did, to an extent, but also a lot of intelligent angry people with legitimate grievances. Some of which were reflected in their own relationship to their Elders. After all, what sort of God of Chaos has an orthodox church as well as inquisition? Its affecting them as much as its affecting them.<br /> <br /> * The Anarchs aren't mentioning it but a lot of the reason for its new aggressive stance as well as rise in success is due to quite a lot of Sabbat Elders defecting. <b>Vasantasena</b> is one of them and has been a major influence on them but it's worrying as it well could mean history repeats itself.<br /> <br /> * <b>Tyler</b> has defected to the Anarchs fully but not for the fact that she's regained her idealistic younger self. It's more that her ties to the Sabbat were exposed and her Blood Bond to Helena broken. As such, she got the hell out of dodge. She's now setting herself up as a Baron of Barons in the movement since the modern Anarchs are actually amendable to &quot;leadership&quot; in a way she's surprised (due to the prevalence of new Gangrel and Brujah members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T14:26:25-08:00","id":1359354,"title":"","content":"Ravnos and Salubri are reforging and alliance of broken clans in India with the Danava (inspiration from DAV Companion). May be this clans could build a new sect for a new setting in the east.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T16:49:48-08:00","id":1359800,"title":"","content":"Dammit, forum ate my post.<br /> <br /> Gonna post this here so I can try to edit this and try to get some of it written down again.<br /> <br /> CAINITES OF THE EAST<br /> <br /> (Disclaimer: A lot of good stuff has been written about the relative merits &amp; flaws of the Kuei-Jin. I personally respect their niche, but think they do have serious issues. Yet this probably isn't the best place to go over those. My group hates them so in my games I usually banish them to a solitary mountain where they play out eternal morality plays. However in general, I'm more or less fine with them to an extent, but I usually change the way I run Asia as a continent from canon due to my and my own group's issues with it. I'm not a scholar of Asian cultures or histories and I can't write up the same quality of posts that some others have about what native Asian vampiric cultures may look like. I can only share what I, myself, tend to do and say that I try to be as respectful as possible and to inform myself as much as I can before I ever present something detailed in-play. Anyway, without further ado, my headcanons...)<br /> <br /> \u2022Asia has vampires. From Jiang-Shi bygones and similar Chi drinkers that somewhat resemble the Laibon &amp; Drowned Legacies in form, to the Kuei-Jin of old infamy, and of course to the damned Children of Caine. The Cainites are naturally not the first vampires of Asia, yet many of been here for so long that only immortals could truly care enough to split hairs...<br /> <br /> \u2022The first Cainites who visited Central &amp; Far East Asia did so during the days of the First and Second City. Caine &amp; Lilith almost certainly spent time their in their prehistoric wandering while forgotten 2nd Gen &amp; Antedeluvians may have sired creatures that one would call the 'Laibon/Drowned Legacies of the East'. Who can say? Yet, we do know that by the time of the Second City, some antediluvians and their exiled children had wandered through. Among the first were of course Ennoia, Ravnos, Saulot, and the Eldest. Wandering kindred in this time would come to reach almost everywhere human feet touched on the globe after all...<br /> <br /> \u2022By the time that the Second City fell and societies began to arise in the Indus River Valley, China, and South East Asia; several kindred lineages were established in Asia. Predominant were the Gangrel, Malkavians, Nosferatu, Ravnos, Salubri, &amp; Tzimisce. In time trade and travel would cause most clans to be represented to some degree, however minute. This allowed a vampiric culture that was somewhat similar politically to the ones of kindred in the Middle East, Northern Africa, &amp; Europe to arise in Asia simultaneously, although naturally distinct as the kindred adapted to and adopted the cultures of their host peoples.<br /> <br /> \u2022History marched on and the kindred reflected their host cultures. Vampires followed the lead of humanity and dark territories were carved across Asia. Regional cultures divided clans between high &amp; low and elders ruled over the young. The kindred learned how to co-exist with the Kuei-Jin and other supernatural through treaties and compromise. The Jyhad waged as ever as grudges, ego, alliances, and treaties spread across Asia much like it had in the west; creating something akin to the War of Princes there as well. What was different however, was that the sheer scale of distance that Asia enjoyed from Europe and its limited contact with the west inured it from the flames of the Inquisition. While the young still revolted against elders, supernaturals still warred, and the humans grew furious with their nocturnal overlords and the Silence of the Blood was founded and kept; the kindred of Asia had neither the opportunity nor inclination to participate in the great experiment of the Camarilla or Sabbat. Sure India had its Jati and certain kindred lineages declared themselves 'Emperors' or 'Magistrates' of great swaths of territory and warred with their neighbors and rebellious childer to maintain their power; yet these kindred never needed adopt the sect culture of the west and this would become the notable difference between East &amp; West that set the stage for the conflict that came following European arrival...<br /> <br /> (I've got more but I'll end this text wall here and add the rest later if people seem interested or the mood strikes me)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","user":"Gryffon15","date":". 01-08-2020, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T10:32:48-08:00","id":1360550,"title":"","content":"Further thoughts &amp; head-canons regarding Asia:<br /> <br /> \u2022The introduction of western kindred to Asia was slow and sparse for a great deal of time, trade routes through the Middle East did connect the continents somewhat, as well as traders along the south seas. The Anda Gangrel who followed the Mongol Invasions further helped create ties between the continents as western Lasombra &amp; Brujah amongst others became aware of vampiric realms beyond their sights. This stewed for a time until the kindred of the west finally had opportunity to expand out from the hoary halls of dusty Europe and followed the kine's imperial adventures into Africa and Asia alike...<br /> <br /> \u2022The Sabbat in Spanish and Portuguese ships were amongst the first western kindred to arrive in Far East Asia and they broke out in hunger for ancient blood and new territories like a plague. The Cainites of Asia were bewildered by these pale newcomers and their so-called 'Crusades' and while some weak domains did fall and the native kindred allowed enemies to fall to the Sabbat amaranth, eventually coalitions formed against these savage invaders and as the Cainites of Asia determined to hold fast to their own domains against Western Invasion, the sails of imperial expansion had brought the Camarilla and Anarch Movement to their shores...<br /> <br /> \u2022Just as China, Japan, India &amp; other nations fought imperialist expansion, so did their native Cainites work to combat the western invaders who sought to envelop them into their War of Sects and unite two branches dynasties of the Jyhad again. While the Camarilla in time would see some successes and adoptions within domains where they could wield mortal institutional powers as Europeans and even in a few domains where the low clans were willing to destroy their ancient masters, though here the Sabbat &amp; Anarchs were far more likely to see successes as they triggered eruptions of unrest and revolt throughout portions of rural East Asia. Despite this though, the western sects were largely a minority position in Asia. The ancient hierarchies remained largely empowered throughout the continent and sub-continent and it was largely only along the coastlines and islands where the Europeans had seen the most success that the western sects could truly claim to be in power. Yet, if nothing else this invasion did one thing, it forced the Kindred of Asia to formalize their web of alliances into something resembling a sect to avoid being turned against each other and destroyed one after another. Thus rose the Black Courts...<br /> <br /> \u2022Something must be noted as far as clans are concerned: Asia is not and was not Europe and as such some things remain that shocked European Kindred upon arrival. For one, while they are few in number, Cappadocians remain in Asia, largely under the guard of their more locally prominent bloodlines, including the Nagaraja. This is likely why the Giovanni have often found themselves viciously contested outside of a few places such as Hong Kong and Tokyo when attempting to claim domain in East Asia while by contrast the Harbingers of Skulls of the Sabbat have something akin to a regional Renaissance. For another thing, Clan Salubri remains. While largely of the Watcher Caste, their Warrior &amp; Healer kin who successfully fled Europe to escape the Tremere do now have places throughout Asian domains as well and so during the western invasions it was the Salubri who championed movements to turn back the western sects and then create the Black Courts, with Asia being considered the most dangerous place in the world to be Tremere. Finally, those Tzimisce lineages here were embraced prior to The Eldest forming their covenant with Kupala, meaning that they largely represent what would be called in Europe 'Old Clan Tzimisce' and thus, with the same vigor the Salubri championed against the Camarilla, these Tzimice championed against the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> \u2022While the Sabbat and Camarilla both have faced incredible challenges while introducing themselves to Asia, another group were able to do such with much more success. The Anarch Movement was better able to spread itself across Asia for two prominent reasons. The first being that Asian Cainites had no memory of the Anarch Revolts to concern them nor did the Movement contain such problematic clans that had created issues for the Camarilla and Sabbat. For another, many Asian Cainites did not recognize the Anarchs as a sect. The Anarch Movement was deemed more akin to a philosophy or ideology, an argument not without some merit, and given the freedom with which ideologies were used to passing across the continent so long as the local ruler was not disturbed and the fierce autonomy that many domains still claimed, the Movement was able to slide like sand through a sieve into Asia while more centralized and solidified sects such as the Camarilla &amp; Sabbat got stuck. This would prove to have disastrous consequences for the Black Courts come the early 20th century as the Anarch Movement ingratiated itself too many young kindred and low clans who chafed under the rule of the high clans and elders both. With an abundant population who slowly became sympathetic to their cause and a mortal movement to draw recruits and inspiration from, the Anarchs struck. As Communism &amp; Republicanism toppled Imperial doctrines throughout Asia, the Anarch Movement raged across the continent and subcontinent, leading something akin to a second great Anarch Revolt. While this revolt did not destroy the Black Courts or old order, it did establish numerous Anarch domains of countless stripes across Asia while destabilizing and forcing the Black Courts to grow more centralized as it began to resemble its western counterpart, the Camarilla. As the 20th century came to its own, just as the new world became a fierce battle ground of the War of Sects &amp; Jyhad, so to did Asia follow in kind...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","user":"Gryffon15","date":". 01-12-2020, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T13:16:03-08:00","id":1360577,"title":"","content":"<b>The WOD and History</b><br /> <br /> * There's a certain level of Pulpiness to the World of Darkness which contrasts against its Gothic Punk horror veneer. This is something that is notable only to its supernatural inhabitants and is a bit of a &quot;dying of the light&quot; against the darkness and shows what the world COULD be like if it could resist the horror beyond.<br /> <br /> * In Ancient Times, vampires often were considered somewhat less malevolent than they are today. A god that demands blood sacrifices, keeps harems of slaves, and is prone to murderous temper tantrums IS a typical god to most cultures. Vampires also did things like controlled the weather, kept away werewolves in the Impergium, and had the few powers capable of healing the sick or injured. Carthage, Mithras, and other vampires come from this view that is less &quot;vampires are damned and dirty forever.&quot; It also, mind you, backfired in some places as we see with some of the bloodiest and most evil gods (Kronos getting diablerized by Zeus for example).<br /> <br /> * Alexander the Great, of all people, helped bring about the end of the age of the god kings. In this reality actually being a demigod (or believing he was a demigod so much he became one) and destroyed dozens of local vampire despots. His generals turned against him when he was either Embraced or they received offers of power that trumped their loyalty.<br /> <br /> * During Medieval times there was a genuine bunch of supernatural soldiers wandering around the world doing the Arthurian thing than there ever was during real life. They fought witches, vampires, and trolls while sometimes also being witches, vampires, and trolls. Sadly, the conflict among them resulted in supernaturals being weakened enough for the Inquisition to slaughter the majority of &quot;good&quot; supernaturals and slander their name. Now the very idea of vampire Pilgrim Knights and so on is derided by even those who are descended from them.<br /> <br /> * The Papal Inquisition gets most of the flack for vampire hunting but it was actually the Protestant Witch Hunters that did the majority of damage. The big difference being that vampires tend to equate all Christians with Catholics (at least at the time) and also that while the Catholic Church's Albergines Crusade and Spanish Inquisition are monstrous, the Protestant Witch Hunts actually tended to be far less discriminate. They did, however, do the most damage by going after supernatural SUPPORT groups. Tens of Thousands of Kinfolk, Kinian, Herds, Ghouls, and Acolytes did more to break the supernatural's power than actual slaying. They also killed about 10 for every person even tangentially related.<br /> <br /> * The French Revolution would have never succeeded without the covert aid of the Anarchs and this applies to many revolts but this is due to the supernatural influence cancelling each other out rather than the reverse. The Reign of Terror, though, was even bloodier and more ridiculous because that's what happens when vampires are in charge of a social movement. They make it worse. Something similar happened with the Bolsheviks but they hardly needed help.<br /> <br /> * There was a steampunk League of Extraordinary Gentleman style period and fantastical Wild West in the 19th century that was far in excess of what happened in RL. Lots more outlaw towns, violent showdowns, and so on than ever was in reality. The Technocracy won against local native wizards and people with the help of the Camarilla, signalling the downfall of traditional power structures of indigenous people and the rise of a world-wide union--or so they thought. Eventually, they were driven out but the scars they left lasted lifetimes and left people no longer believing in their local heroes. Yes, there's a pattern of heroics getting smashed down, why do you ask?<br /> <br /> * World War 1...was not remotely supernatural. Indeed, it is one of the least supernatural wars of all time.<br /> <br /> * WW2 was every bit as Pulpy and full of wackiness as you'd expect with Nazi mad scientists, armies of zombies, Satanic cults holding torch-lit ceremonies in crumbling castles, and the Technocracy as well as Traditions openly collaborating with the governments. The irony being that as far as the Nazis knew, most of these groups weren't actually under their control. They all believed they were in command of the fascists (or allies) but mostly just lent their aid while believing they would rule the world in the end. Hitler may have been actually replaced and killed a couple of times but if it walks like a duck and talks like a duck, is it really not a duck?<br /> <br /> * WW2 was also the last time supernaturals overtly played an important role in military history. Alan Turing was the last openly supernatural person of importance and killed for that (as well as homophobia among the Technocracy). Now supernaturals operate almost entirely through proxy groups like Anonymous and the Virtual Adepts or Occupy Wallstreet (as well as the Tea party) for the Brujah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-12-2020, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T20:29:58-08:00","id":1360630,"title":"","content":"These are cool CTP! I'm gonna consider adopting some of that!<br /> <br /> Now, to detour from my usual essay about why Cainites in Asia is cool, here's a more Western headcanon that came to me on my car ride home today and I really liked.<br /> <br /> THE PEACE OF KINGS<br /> <br /> \u2022In the time of the First City, Caine was King and Enoch was the Prince for whom the city bore the name. Caine was first amongst the Damned, yet he had been cursed by The One Above and he knew that to claim the title of 'King' was to insult The One, yet in his spite he readily did so. This was another instrument of his tragedy.<br /> <br /> \u2022By the end of Enoch Caine had proclaimed his rulings, wisdom, and warnings which his children gathered in the Book of Nod. Amongst these warnings is that none should call themselves 'god' and the tradition arose that only Caine himself would be called 'King', for any other to do so would be usurpation and while [Ventrue] and [Lasombra] were willing to throw down Enoch to be called 'Prince', neither desired to fight and be destroyed by their grand-sire, whom remained King.<br /> <br /> \u2022The Children of Caine were rebellious and spiteful as Caine himself was towards his Maker. The antediluvians called themselves gods in the time of the Second City and only by its destruction did they realize the truth of Caine's warning, that The One Above was a Jealous God and would never endure those damned such as them to be called 'god' and rule over humanity. Yet, their children rebuked their sire's wisdom, and proclaimed themselves gods again in the first cities of man after the Deluge and Fall of Ubar (Second City). Those who did would soon find themselves emerged in great tragedy, tribulation, and often truly destroyed. As blood gods fell to ash forever, the tumultuous children sought for an answer and they found one in the warnings of their elders and the Book of Nod. The One Above would never tolerate them as gods, so godship they rebuked. Yet this would not be their final time of suffering for their own arrogance.<br /> <br /> \u2022While the Children of Caine had largely learned that they could not be gods, their arrogance did not cease, it merely transformed. They ruled the night with fabulous power, so they must be recognized. If not as gods, then as kings. So these children ruled as kings in Assyria, Mycae, Egypt, and all across Creation and for a time they rejoiced in bloody reigns and indulgences until again ruin befell them and they desperately sought the reason why. The Noddists rebuked these night kings for claiming titles not their own. Neither Caine nor The One Above had granted them kingship and if they wished to avoid another great Deluge or personal destruction, they must turn it aside. So, those who remained, greatly upset, did so turn away from kingly things. They claimed the titles of 'Prince' so as to not displease their Dark Father and they chose shadows so as to avoid the gaze of The One Above. Yet not all...<br /> <br /> \u2022Legends say that proud Set was the last vampire who refused to forsake his crown and was thus struck dead by The One Above and/or Caine. This is unlikely as many reports show that Set had faded into the shadows by the beginning of the Pharonic age. Ones who did remain ruling as open blood gods and kings were Troile and Moloch in Carthage and the greatest Cassandra seers of Rome predicted untold ruin if Carthage remained. So Rome rose its legions and marched with Ventrue at its head and they destroyed the city and cast down its false gods to avoid destruction themselves. So some of the romans say at least. Regardless, vampires were no longer gods nor kings. Yet, as Rome saw, vampires controlled kings and priests. The false humility of these 'Princes' was magnificent to see and the vain kindred luxuriated in their triumph. Rome was the perfection of vampirism within the Order of The One Above, Caine, &amp; Nod as well as all gods. Yet Rome fell...<br /> <br /> \u2022Some blame Lasombra treachery. Some blame Ventrue arrogance. Some blame Toreador decadence. Some blame Gangrel brutality. Some blame Malkavian madness. Some blame Brujah vengeance. Some even blame those who did not heed Caine's supposed warnings that his children must never tolerate those who worshiped The One Above in their midst and say that Rome fell the day that Jews and Christians walked its streets unmolested. Regardless Rome did fall and its fall seemed apocalyptic. It seemed like Gehenna. Some Noddists proclaimed it to be the third fall. First gods, then kings, then princes who ruled kings. All these things had threatened a ruin that had finally come. Others claim that Rome fell for a hundred reasons, all mundane. Regardless, the seeds of The Peace of Kings was born here in the fertile soil left by The Gehenna of Rome and The Book of Nod.<br /> <br /> \u2022Europe rebuilt itself and so did the kindred. They were proud and eternal and thus determined to rise again. So they did. The dark ages witnessed the Courts of Love, the Voivodate, the Black Fiefs, Mithran Britain, The Constantinian Dream, and Ashirra; amongst numerous others. The kindred rose again and they did so whispering in the ears of kings, bishops, and all other great men and women they could. As they grew in power and control, corruption grew rampant and the world became a chessboard for the petty conflicts of the Jyhad which used kings and kingdoms as its pieces. This War of Princes plunged the World into ever deepening spirals of misery, trapped childer within the cruel chains of their elders, and made mortals slave to nocturnal overlords. Perhaps if the Noddists had not been so preoccupied with mourning Rome they would have seen the signs of what was to come...<br /> <br /> \u2022All the proud trappings with which they had rebuilt the splendor of Rome erupted into flame and crumbled into ashes with the Inquisition. The Cainites had pressed too much upon the kine, kings and peasants alike refused to live in fear. The Lasombra were discovered within the heart of The Church and faith in her cracked in ways that shattered Europe even further and drove Her stewards to adopt the Inquisition and redeem themselves in the flames of zeal. Childer who had been pressed into slavery and lorded over by tyrannic elders erupted into revolt as Anarch Revolts shook Europe. The Doom of the Salubri, The Fall of Constantinople, the Black Death. Europe heaved and the War of Princes imploded upon itself as Europe blazed. Only as the fires began to fade could those who remained come together in shaken horror. To make a pact so that this may never come again. Some chose the veil of secrecy, the society of their fellows and its protections; they authored the Camarilla. Some others chose the threat of terror, the society of free monsters; they authored the Sabbat. Some walked the paths they always had. Regardless though, whether they called it The First Tradition or The Silence of the Blood; all who survived heeded the Masquerade...<br /> <br /> \u2022In the debates that forged The Masquerade, another pact was made. A pact made as Noddists observed the trends of the Second City, Carthage, and Rome repeated over again. Debates that were theological and secular, practical and traditional. From these debates, another pact would be made. The Peace of Kings.<br /> <br /> Never more would kindred rule openly. Never more would they rule the kine with an iron fist and fangs bared. Perhaps Kings truly were empowered by Divine Right and protected by The One Above, perhaps they were simply unwilling to suffer abuse like they had in the War of Princes all over again. Regardless the pact was made. From those nights on, kindred would no longer control, only influence. No longer direct, only sway. No longer rule as kings, only whisper as princes.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat would reject The Peace but in time they would be forced to accept it out of necessity, out of the coalition that rose up to defend the kings and out of the fact that kings and queens now knew how to reject them. Not until they were forgotten could they try again to rule as once before and by then it would be too late. These new kings would have new protectors and the cost of assailing them would be too high. Those who loathed The Peace would bide their day. Whether tomorrow or at Gehenna, they say, it will fail and they will rule again. Perhaps.<br /> <br /> Yet, The Peace of Kings remains. Vampires do not whisper to The Pope. Vampires do not dictate to Prime Ministers. Vampires do not command Presidents. Now... perhaps they bribe politicians, perhaps they seduce congressman, perhaps they blackmail generals... yet only to influence. Never to control.<br /> <br /> That is simply what noble monsters do...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","user":"Gryffon15","date":". 01-13-2020, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T13:37:50-08:00","id":1360742,"title":"","content":"-Ubar was the first home of the Baali, the location of the original Pit where the tree was spawned. Time has covered memories with dust, and It has been confused with the first city, but it was never that.<br /> <br /> In the real world history, Ubar was a city in the &quot;empty quarter&quot; area of Arabia also know as Irem. It grew at a large oasis where trade routes intersected. As it grew, it drew more and more water from the ground, dropping the water table and leaving it resting on porous ground. In the end the entire fortress of Ubar collapsed onto a monstrous sinkhole. A city that collapsed into a gigantic pit is just too Baali to ignore","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T12:32:20-08:00","id":1360922,"title":"","content":"I believe the Harbingers and Nagaraja joined together with a conversation roughly like this:<br /> <br /> True Hand: You are free, Harbingers! Free from the Underworld!<br /> <br /> Harbinger: Ecstatic! Thank you guys. We owe you big.<br /> <br /> True Hand: Yes, the true children of Cappadocias are free!<br /> <br /> Harbinger: Oh, yeah, about that. Fuck Cappadocias.<br /> <br /> True Hand: Pardon?<br /> <br /> Harbinger: Yeah, that piece of shit fucked us over bad. Also, the Antediluvians hated each other. Believe me, most of us are old enough to know this.<br /> <br /> True Hand: But...but...<br /> <br /> Harbinger: We owe you big but, yeah, he was insane. So are all of them. You should steer the fuck clear of them.<br /> <br /> Nagaraja: Actually, there's this Beckoning thing we're scared of. The True Hand also let the Baali join.<br /> <br /> Harbinger: Say what?<br /> <br /> Nagaraja: Can we join you, instead?<br /> <br /> Harbinger: ....yes. Also, True Hand, uh...we owe you but....never call us again.<br /> <br /> True Hand: But these Baali are cool!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T13:34:43-08:00","id":1360943,"title":"","content":"Harbinger: (fiddling with the smart phone) Say, is there an app that would let me block the True Hand, but without them knowing I've blocked them?<br /> <br /> Nagaraja: Yes, but the Baali are the one's who made the app.<br /> <br /> Harbinger: Damn it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T19:40:46-08:00","id":1361002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1360577#post1360577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* In Ancient Times, vampires often were considered somewhat less malevolent than they are today. A god that demands blood sacrifices, keeps harems of slaves, and is prone to murderous temper tantrums IS a typical god to most cultures. Vampires also did things like controlled the weather, kept away werewolves in the Impergium, and had the few powers capable of healing the sick or injured. Carthage, Mithras, and other vampires come from this view that is less &quot;vampires are damned and dirty forever.&quot; It also, mind you, backfired in some places as we see with some of the bloodiest and most evil gods (Kronos getting diablerized by Zeus for example).<br /> <br /> * Alexander the Great, of all people, helped bring about the end of the age of the god kings. In this reality actually being a demigod (or believing he was a demigod so much he became one) and destroyed dozens of local vampire despots. His generals turned against him when he was either Embraced or they received offers of power that trumped their loyalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like you could consider it a westernized version of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Shih\" target=\"_blank\">Yi the Archer</a> who was the creator of the Shih and also a mage (or a hedge magician at least) who didn't know he was tapping into magical power for the amazing things he did (like killing other supernaturals.) Given a 'fractured cosmos' view of things, you could see them being different 'aspects' of the same entity muddled by time and myth.<br /> <br /> Alternately a superhuman Alexander might work well with the idea of being some super-Imbued (the ancient heroes and their blood wre more powerful than the modern, weaker 'hunters')<br /> <br /> Or you could just take a page from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reign:_The_Conqueror\" target=\"_blank\">Reign the Conqueror</a>. That was fairly supernatural and that Alexander was pretty crazy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * During Medieval times there was a genuine bunch of supernatural soldiers wandering around the world doing the Arthurian thing than there ever was during real life. They fought witches, vampires, and trolls while sometimes also being witches, vampires, and trolls. Sadly, the conflict among them resulted in supernaturals being weakened enough for the Inquisition to slaughter the majority of &quot;good&quot; supernaturals and slander their name. Now the very idea of vampire Pilgrim Knights and so on is derided by even those who are descended from them. </div> </div> </div>This seems to be begging for a crossover between a Grail Knight and their ghouls, a couple of Salubri, some Changelings, and some mages.<br /> <br /> You could possibly even throw in the proto-Imbued that became Inquisitors in the Dark Ages (maybe a couple were part of this supernatural Knights of the Round Table, only to leave it and join the Church and Inquisition and forge the Dark Ages Inquisitors.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * There was a steampunk League of Extraordinary Gentleman style period and fantastical Wild West in the 19th century that was far in excess of what happened in RL. Lots more outlaw towns, violent showdowns, and so on than ever was in reality. The Technocracy won against local native wizards and people with the help of the Camarilla, signalling the downfall of traditional power structures of indigenous people and the rise of a world-wide union--or so they thought. Eventually, they were driven out but the scars they left lasted lifetimes and left people no longer believing in their local heroes. Yes, there's a pattern of heroics getting smashed down, why do you ask? </div> </div> </div>If we're going the route of LxG and Steampunk why not make it more European vs American? Sort of a supernatural version of the American revolution. American kindred might be proto-Anarchs (or perhaps the proto-Sabbat migrated in large numbers to America to form their own base of operations and get away from the stuck up Euro Camarilla) and they're busy trying to forge some sort of settlement among other supernaturals (werewolf already had a wild west setting, and steampunk is just begging for the Sons of Ether.)<br /> <br /> IIRC the technocracy of this time aren't as fully established (or rigid) as they become later, so they might be more unwitting pawns for the Euro Camarilla in trying to wage war/conquer the Americas.<br /> <br /> Also Sherlock Holmes should meet the WoD Dracula. Somehow. For even bigger pulp and steampunkiness make him a <a href=\"https://bravestarr.fandom.com/wiki/Sherlock_Holmes\" target=\"_blank\">Time travelling Detective</a> with <a href=\"https://html\" target=\"_blank\">lightning powers</a>. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","user":"Mister_Dunpeal","date":". 01-14-2020, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T00:41:55-08:00","id":1361025,"title":"","content":"Various horror fictions in our world may be treated as documentaries or dramatic reenactments of events in the WoD. These include <i>Nightmare on Elm Street, Texas Chainsaw Massacre</i>, the podcast <i>The White Vault</i>, and the novel <i>Carrie</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T04:38:05-08:00","id":1361054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1361025#post1361025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Various horror fictions in our world may be treated as documentaries or dramatic reenactments of events in the WoD. These include <i>Nightmare on Elm Street, Texas Chainsaw Massacre</i>, the podcast <i>The White Vault</i>, and the novel <i>Carrie</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's basically the premise of THE RISE OF LESLIE VERNON. Slashers are a real thing even if no one believes they're supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T07:39:55-08:00","id":1361078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1361025#post1361025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Various horror fictions in our world may be treated as documentaries or dramatic reenactments of events in the WoD. These include <i>Nightmare on Elm Street, Texas Chainsaw Massacre</i>, the podcast <i>The White Vault</i>, and the novel <i>Carrie</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, Leatherface and Freddie would fit better in CofD, I think. White Vault I can see as an Imbued-affiliated underground network. Carrie... either a nascent psychic or a hedge witch would be my guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T11:23:31-08:00","id":1361114,"title":"","content":"I've used slashers in a WoD game before. They're a perfect fit. <br /> <br /> That's an interesting thought so far as marrying them with the Imbued, though. Both have the same &quot;functionally human, but more than human&quot; shtick going for them. And as of CofD 2e, hunters who really lose it are supposed to become slashers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T11:34:15-08:00","id":1361121,"title":"","content":"On that tangent, some more CofD ideas stolen for WoD:<br /> <br /> Marcus Vitel is one of my favorite NPCs, but his bio felt like he spent 2,000 years twiddling his thumbs until he got to be prince of D.C. There's a ton of possible history in his unlife to fill in. One chapter: Requiem for Rome floats the idea that amidst the endless succession of 3rd century emperors who bribed the Praetorian Guard to kill the current emperor and make them the new emperor, there's a vampire who simply ghouls the Praetorian Guard and declares himself emperor. Guess who? Marcus Vitel. This is the same vampire who wants to start a nuclear war to kill the Antediluvians, so &quot;ridiculously over the top&quot; is his MO.<br /> <br /> Vitel naturally believed his rule wouldn't go unopposed, but he figured the methuselahs in Rome's Eternal Senate were tired of the caesars dying practically the day they seized the throne, and would appreciate a more stable immortal emperor who was still &quot;young&quot; (Vitel was ~200) and inexperienced enough for them to manipulate. Only, after sweet-talking the Eternal Senate, Vitel neglected to mention he had no plans on being anyone's pawn. Power went to his head and he tried to play the various methuselahs against one another before they finally tired of his games, decided Vitel as emperor wasn't working out, and united to depose him. He barely fled with his unlife, but swore that ultimate power would again be his. <br /> <br /> Also, that he'd get to call himself &quot;emperor&quot; again some night too...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T11:59:39-08:00","id":1361128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1361078#post1361078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, Leatherface and Freddie would fit better in CofD, I think. White Vault I can see as an Imbued-affiliated underground network. Carrie... either a nascent psychic or a hedge witch would be my guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>My points were A. the WoD is a deeply toxic and dangerous place, full of hateful predators, B vampires are not the only predator about and plenty of the others will utterly fuck up any vampires they encounter.<br /> <br /> Edit: If I had to nail everything down in terms of game mechanics, Michael Myers is imbued, Leatherface is not he just has a support system in the form of his family, Jason is some manner of fomori or spectre driven risen, and Kruger is a spectre. So, out of that, only one is imbued.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 01-15-2020, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T12:21:21-08:00","id":1361132,"title":"","content":"A swift adaptation:<br /> <br /> * Jason Voorhees: Risen<br /> <br /> * Freddy: Specter with Dream Manipulation<br /> <br /> * Michael Meyers: Human (he's just really really evil)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T14:42:38-08:00","id":1361166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1361002#post1361002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like you could consider it a westernized version of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Shih\" target=\"_blank\">Yi the Archer</a> who was the creator of the Shih and also a mage (or a hedge magician at least) who didn't know he was tapping into magical power for the amazing things he did (like killing other supernaturals.) Given a 'fractured cosmos' view of things, you could see them being different 'aspects' of the same entity muddled by time and myth.<br /> <br /> Alternately a superhuman Alexander might work well with the idea of being some super-Imbued (the ancient heroes and their blood wre more powerful than the modern, weaker 'hunters')</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, I've always had the idea of Mages being the secret &quot;protectors of humanity&quot; and their powers manifesting in different ways as well. A mage who believes themselves to be a god has potential power well beyond that. But so is a Super-Imbued as well. I actually have introduced Imbued into my games as humans possessed by Demon: The Fallen-esque Angels but the Redemption obsessed ones. Basically, I don't go with normal rules but make them FUCKING TERRIFYING.<br /> <br /> Like you're playing V:TM and then suddenly Simon Belmont shows up and starts throwing glowing crosses and swinging a whip made of fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or you could just take a page from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reign:_The_Conqueror\" target=\"_blank\">Reign the Conqueror</a>. That was fairly supernatural and that Alexander was pretty crazy. </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be surprised if there weren't other figures every bit as important as Alexander in overthrowing vampire god kings but it certainly is how it's remembered among Europe and many Middle Eastern Kindred in my games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This seems to be begging for a crossover between a Grail Knight and their ghouls, a couple of Salubri, some Changelings, and some mages. </div> </div> </div>Indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You could possibly even throw in the proto-Imbued that became Inquisitors in the Dark Ages (maybe a couple were part of this supernatural Knights of the Round Table, only to leave it and join the Church and Inquisition and forge the Dark Ages Inquisitors.) </div> </div> </div>The Imbued showing up in the Inquisition is a pretty easy and interesting merging actually as it would go a long way to exposing why so many vampires could be found and destroyed. While I think humans are perfectly capable of destroying the undead and this is why I support the Second Inquisition (just to show, &quot;yes, this is why the Masquerade exists&quot;), you could easily have hunters with the Sight show up and slaughter many many supernaturals then go away when their numbers are reduced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we're going the route of LxG and Steampunk why not make it more European vs American? Sort of a supernatural version of the American revolution. American kindred might be proto-Anarchs (or perhaps the proto-Sabbat migrated in large numbers to America to form their own base of operations and get away from the stuck up Euro Camarilla) and they're busy trying to forge some sort of settlement among other supernaturals (werewolf already had a wild west setting, and steampunk is just begging for the Sons of Ether.)<br /> <br /> IIRC the technocracy of this time aren't as fully established (or rigid) as they become later, so they might be more unwitting pawns for the Euro Camarilla in trying to wage war/conquer the Americas. </div> </div> </div>Mainly because I was envisioning native mystics as the kind of people who'd love to fight the Comstocks and their flying cities of the world. Local heroes trying to do battle against imperialism and oppression. But sure, you could do that too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-15-2020, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T16:04:26-08:00","id":1361177,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>Stephen King died at an early age from a spider bite. He never wrote any novels and no one replaced him.</li> <li>J.R.R. Tolkien died from an illness during WWI. He never wrote any novels and no one replaced him.</li> <li>Paulo Coelho, Mitch Albom, Jim Henson, Jerry Siegel, Joe Shuster, Boss Ross, George Lucas, Gene Roddenberry, Stan Lee, Dave Arneson, John Muir, Chico Mendez, and Billy Wilder all died \u2013 often murdered at a young age \u2013 before they ever made any contributions to society or culture.</li> <li>However, Walt Disney, Gary Gygax, Bob Kane, Frank Miller, John Norman and Uwe Boll all went on to long lives working for one Pentex subsidiary or another and all continue to make major contributions to society.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T16:09:52-08:00","id":1361178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1352276-crazy-and-mundane-headcanons-for-v5?p=1361177#post1361177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Stephen King died at an early age from a spider bite. He never wrote any novels and no one replaced him.</li> <li>J.R.R. Tolkien died from an illness during WWI. He never wrote any novels and no one replaced him.</li> <li>Paulo Coelho, Mitch Albom, Jim Henson, Jerry Siegel, Joe Shuster, Boss Ross, George Lucas, Gene Roddenberry, Stan Lee, Dave Arneson, John Muir, Chico Mendez, and Billy Wilder all died \u2013 often murdered at a young age \u2013 before they ever made any contributions to society or culture.</li> <li>However, Walt Disney, Gary Gygax, Bob Kane, Frank Miller, John Norman and Uwe Boll all went on to long lives working for one Pentex subsidiary or another and all continue to make major contributions to society.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Walt Disney is, according to Los Angeles by Night, a member of the Technocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blan